WEBVTT

1
00:01:12.057 --> 00:01:13.677
Oh, yeah.

2
00:01:23.897 --> 00:01:25.697
Don't worry about that, father.

3
00:01:25.777 --> 00:01:27.137
We'll be going soon.

4
00:01:29.377 --> 00:01:31.217
John did you feed them?

5
00:01:31.317 --> 00:01:32.477
Yes son.

6
00:01:32.557 --> 00:01:33.217
Yes.

7
00:01:33.297 --> 00:01:34.517
All right.

8
00:01:34.597 --> 00:01:36.477
Now tighten her up son.

9
00:01:36.557 --> 00:01:38.498
She'll take us where we're going.

10
00:01:39.677 --> 00:01:41.557
Yes but where are we going?

11
00:01:41.637 --> 00:01:44.677
No more. They're thrashing
that matter out over there now.

12
00:01:44.757 --> 00:01:46.677
Pa they made you the leader.

13
00:01:46.757 --> 00:01:48.117
Why don't you say where to go?

14
00:01:48.197 --> 00:01:50.657
I'm only leader of the
Missourians daughter.

15
00:01:50.737 --> 00:01:53.757
Their families here from every
state of the union I reckon.

16
00:01:53.837 --> 00:01:55.537
Can't be waiting on them forever dad.

17
00:01:55.617 --> 00:01:56.557
No son.

18
00:01:56.637 --> 00:01:58.657
They'll hold the tower over there now.

19
00:01:58.737 --> 00:02:01.796
I'll just step over and
see what they've got to say.

20
00:02:03.597 --> 00:02:07.017
Well, bless our wild hearts.

21
00:02:07.277 --> 00:02:08.357
Leave it in.

22
00:02:08.437 --> 00:02:11.177
Great cold. How are you, Zeke?

23
00:02:11.257 --> 00:02:14.457
Well, ask you to hide
yourself what I see, boy.

24
00:02:14.537 --> 00:02:16.117
Been down Santa Fe way, Zeke.

25
00:02:16.197 --> 00:02:17.457
Just drifted in.

26
00:02:17.577 --> 00:02:21.077
Here's Wendy Bell. Looks like
you've went through in good shape.

27
00:02:21.157 --> 00:02:25.357
Well, Coleman, most times I
went through in fair shape.

28
00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:29.717
I'd only put on 60 pounds.

29
00:02:33.097 --> 00:02:36.497
He may be the colors of a
likely stretch of country.

30
00:02:36.797 --> 00:02:41.137
Ray, would you side us to a second
Missouri anywhere out yonder?

31
00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:43.597
Sure.

32
00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:46.877
But it's a long, tough pull from here.

33
00:02:47.037 --> 00:02:50.257
2,500 miles away you'd have to go.

34
00:02:51.477 --> 00:02:53.457
No, it's too far off.

35
00:02:53.537 --> 00:02:56.008
No place is too far if it's what you want.

36
00:02:56.637 --> 00:03:00.497
land beyond Oregon. There ain't
no land beyond Oregon, mister.

37
00:03:00.577 --> 00:03:03.697
Lest to Oregon comes the ocean,
the way it's been told to me.

38
00:03:03.777 --> 00:03:05.457
This stretch is north of Oregon.

39
00:03:05.537 --> 00:03:07.617
How many people settled on it now?

40
00:03:07.997 --> 00:03:09.397
It's Indian country.

41
00:03:09.477 --> 00:03:13.317
Except for the trappers, never a
white man has left his track there.

42
00:03:13.397 --> 00:03:15.877
Only one trading post
in that whole country.

43
00:03:15.957 --> 00:03:18.237
Who owns it? A Missouri trapper owner.

44
00:03:18.317 --> 00:03:20.157
Hey, mister, will you tell me this?

45
00:03:20.237 --> 00:03:21.237
Hey, there.

46
00:03:22.017 --> 00:03:26.311
Since you all elected me to he coo
to this outfit, let me do the talking.

47
00:03:26.637 --> 00:03:29.197
It's everything a
Missouri park could crave.

48
00:03:29.277 --> 00:03:33.897
There's two snow-capped mountain
ranges with peaks lost in the sky.

49
00:03:33.977 --> 00:03:37.937
And between them ranges,
men, is a great valley.

50
00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:40.017
Lakes and streams everywhere.

51
00:03:40.097 --> 00:03:42.117
Fish, you ask, and game.

52
00:03:42.197 --> 00:03:46.157
There's salmon swarming up them rivers
thicker than blackbirds in the Cane Plains.

53
00:03:46.237 --> 00:03:48.997
Wren, will you undertake
the leaders to that valley?

54
00:03:49.077 --> 00:03:51.317
I'd like nothing better, men.

55
00:03:52.037 --> 00:03:54.357
But our trail is forked here.

56
00:03:54.457 --> 00:03:57.717
I've got business that calls me
back down the road to Santa Fe.

57
00:03:57.797 --> 00:03:59.677
What business you for, friend?

58
00:03:59.757 --> 00:04:04.217
I'm a trapper. Well, surely they spur
plenty out in that land beyond Oregon.

59
00:04:04.297 --> 00:04:05.297
Plenty.

60
00:04:05.957 --> 00:04:08.957
But I gotta kill me a pair of skunks.

61
00:04:09.157 --> 00:04:11.797
Back a piece on the road to Santa Fe.

62
00:04:12.137 --> 00:04:13.577
Wait, wait.

63
00:04:13.677 --> 00:04:15.977
How do you find that valley?

64
00:04:16.197 --> 00:04:21.079
Well, Mara is sending a bull train clear
through the old Tom Williams trading post.

65
00:04:21.197 --> 00:04:23.777
This is the first time
it's ever been tried.

66
00:04:23.857 --> 00:04:27.117
You string along behind them,
and if they make it through,

67
00:04:27.197 --> 00:04:28.937
you'll find your valley.

68
00:04:29.057 --> 00:04:31.881
And tell that great white
mountain hello for me.

69
00:04:32.217 --> 00:04:33.757
Goodbye, Zeke.

70
00:04:35.937 --> 00:04:36.977
Hey,

71
00:04:39.377 --> 00:04:42.037
maybe he's got up a fairy there.

72
00:04:59.237 --> 00:05:00.657
That's all right.

73
00:05:00.737 --> 00:05:02.257
Now, don't be a pig, you know.

74
00:05:02.337 --> 00:05:03.797
Howdy, Mrs. Riggs.

75
00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.197
Land sakes!

76
00:05:08.677 --> 00:05:11.057
Well, you sure look fine, Mother Riggs.

77
00:05:11.137 --> 00:05:13.717
It's a long time since I've seen you.

78
00:05:13.797 --> 00:05:16.637
You know, you always was
a great hand to wander.

79
00:05:16.717 --> 00:05:18.477
Yeah, I rambled around.

80
00:05:18.837 --> 00:05:20.597
And how are the little twins?

81
00:05:20.677 --> 00:05:22.837
Little? My land.

82
00:05:23.877 --> 00:05:25.457
since you seen them last.

83
00:05:25.537 --> 00:05:26.537
No.

84
00:05:26.817 --> 00:05:28.677
They in the house? Mildred is.

85
00:05:28.757 --> 00:05:30.777
Elise went down to watch the boat come in.

86
00:05:30.857 --> 00:05:33.117
I reckon I'll saunter
in and surprise Mildred.

87
00:05:33.197 --> 00:05:35.457
Oh, you sure will surprise us.

88
00:05:55.297 --> 00:05:58.857
Oh, Rebecca, I sure am glad to see you.

89
00:05:58.937 --> 00:06:03.157
Well, Mildred, you certainly have
doubled in size since last I saw you.

90
00:06:03.237 --> 00:06:04.937
You just must see Elise.

91
00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:08.332
Don't worry, I'll drop back
and see her before I leave.

92
00:06:09.017 --> 00:06:10.977
That's the theme of
the bell whistling now.

93
00:06:11.057 --> 00:06:12.277
Holy, thank you.

94
00:06:30.057 --> 00:06:33.317
Well, Miss Cameron, we'll
be landing in a few minutes.

95
00:06:33.397 --> 00:06:34.517
Got all you outfit together?

96
00:06:34.597 --> 00:06:36.137
Look, everything's ready, Captain Harper.

97
00:06:36.217 --> 00:06:40.597
Listen, why don't you give
up this plan and turn back?

98
00:06:40.677 --> 00:06:43.777
Why, there's no place to turn back soon.

99
00:06:43.857 --> 00:06:47.237
Why, there's no home in all the thousands
that wouldn't welcome the daughter of

100
00:06:47.317 --> 00:06:51.257
Colonel Cameron. True, we can
hardly become a happy citizen.

101
00:06:51.337 --> 00:06:53.777
It's a tough proposition, girls.

102
00:06:53.857 --> 00:06:56.497
There's pioneer life
in a savage wilderness.

103
00:06:56.577 --> 00:07:00.937
We realize that, Captain Hollister,
but we must keep the family together.

104
00:07:01.017 --> 00:07:02.677
Honey girl wants to stay with us.

105
00:07:02.757 --> 00:07:07.457
And our brother Dave's almost a man-grown.

106
00:07:07.737 --> 00:07:09.577
Ruth is right, Captain.

107
00:07:22.017 --> 00:07:25.157
Are you still determined
to be a sturdy pioneer?

108
00:07:25.237 --> 00:07:27.397
Quite determined, Mr. Thorpe.

109
00:07:27.937 --> 00:07:31.777
I told you about my
plantation in Louisiana.

110
00:07:31.857 --> 00:07:33.657
It must be wonderful.

111
00:07:33.997 --> 00:07:36.877
Miss Cameron, those lands
and servants are you.

112
00:07:37.517 --> 00:07:39.437
Did you take me with me?

113
00:07:39.517 --> 00:07:43.717
Oh, I do thank you, but as I've
said before, it's quite impossible.

114
00:07:43.957 --> 00:07:45.737
Goodbye, Mrs. Thorne.

115
00:08:03.117 --> 00:08:07.537
Oh, Davy, I think I'd better go find this
safe that Navy Captain Hollister told us

116
00:08:07.617 --> 00:08:11.337
about. All right. Now I want to
stay in the state and find my house.

117
00:08:11.417 --> 00:08:13.377
Well, you take good care of it, baby.

118
00:08:13.457 --> 00:08:15.751
I will. I'll be right back, honey girl.

119
00:08:18.417 --> 00:08:20.437
It's a nice place, isn't it, Mama?

120
00:08:21.077 --> 00:08:22.297
It's terrible.

121
00:08:22.437 --> 00:08:24.537
Look at the mud. But listen, Mama.

122
00:08:24.617 --> 00:08:26.257
I'm going to go see if I can buy a horse.

123
00:08:26.337 --> 00:08:28.137
Come on. Come on. I carry you over, Sarah.

124
00:08:28.217 --> 00:08:29.577
I don't want you to get your feet wet.

125
00:08:29.657 --> 00:08:31.437
That's it. Here we go.

126
00:08:38.497 --> 00:08:39.957
Come on, Abby.

127
00:08:41.997 --> 00:08:43.397
Come on, Mama.

128
00:08:50.697 --> 00:08:52.037
Come on, Mama.

129
00:08:52.257 --> 00:08:53.857
Take you over, Mama.

130
00:08:57.277 --> 00:08:58.217
Here!

131
00:08:58.297 --> 00:09:00.257
What are you trying to do?

132
00:09:04.137 --> 00:09:05.937
I'll cross my own mud.

133
00:09:06.017 --> 00:09:07.677
All right then, Mama. But let me help you.

134
00:09:07.757 --> 00:09:08.917
That's it, Mama. Come on, now.

135
00:09:08.997 --> 00:09:11.409
Step in that ward, Mama. That's it, Mama.

136
00:09:13.377 --> 00:09:15.637
Hey, hey, hey, come right back.

137
00:09:19.237 --> 00:09:20.837
Mrs. Biggs.

138
00:09:21.377 --> 00:09:23.177
Yes, miss? That's me.

139
00:09:23.257 --> 00:09:24.817
Well, I'm Miss Cameron.

140
00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:27.137
Captain Hollister told me to see you.

141
00:09:27.217 --> 00:09:28.497
Friend of Captain Hollister?

142
00:09:28.577 --> 00:09:30.777
Yes, I am. Come right on in.

143
00:09:30.857 --> 00:09:33.957
Now, I don't tell you you're
pretty good about this long.

144
00:09:34.037 --> 00:09:35.037
Oh,

145
00:09:39.557 --> 00:09:41.717
now it's cool in here, Alton.

146
00:09:52.717 --> 00:09:55.877
Now you sit down, make yourself easy,
and I'll draw you a cup of tea.

147
00:09:55.957 --> 00:09:57.717
Oh, that's awfully nice of you, Mr.

148
00:09:57.797 --> 00:09:59.697
Hanks. Thanks very much.

149
00:10:16.097 --> 00:10:19.857
What do you mean by...

150
00:10:19.977 --> 00:10:21.677
Oh, I thought...

151
00:10:22.637 --> 00:10:25.937
It was this way. I thought
you were someone else.

152
00:10:26.557 --> 00:10:27.577
Wait.

153
00:10:27.997 --> 00:10:30.697
It was this way. I thought
you were Elise, ma'am.

154
00:10:30.777 --> 00:10:31.277
Elise?

155
00:10:31.277 --> 00:10:33.297
Yes, just thought I'd
surprise her, sort of.

156
00:10:33.377 --> 00:10:34.677
Did you indeed?

157
00:10:35.377 --> 00:10:38.417
Let me tell you. It was this way.

158
00:10:39.837 --> 00:10:42.697
If you'll light someplace, I'll tell you.

159
00:10:49.497 --> 00:10:50.497
Oh,

160
00:10:50.917 --> 00:10:52.597
what is it you're as pale as it goes?

161
00:10:52.677 --> 00:10:54.437
Oh, it's nothing, Mr. Topp, really.

162
00:10:54.517 --> 00:10:56.177
But there must be something wrong.

163
00:10:56.257 --> 00:10:58.697
Nothing, just an unpleasant occurrence.

164
00:10:58.777 --> 00:10:59.997
I'm going to explain that place.

165
00:11:00.077 --> 00:11:01.417
There's nothing to explain.

166
00:11:01.497 --> 00:11:02.817
But I'm going to tell you anyhow.

167
00:11:02.897 --> 00:11:05.257
It seems to me you're
forcing yourself on this lady.

168
00:11:05.337 --> 00:11:06.657
Is that how it seems to you?

169
00:11:06.737 --> 00:11:09.897
How else can I take it? It's
nothing to me how you take it.

170
00:11:09.977 --> 00:11:13.137
But it matters a heap to me,
ma'am, how you understand.

171
00:11:13.217 --> 00:11:16.717
But if it concerns Miss Cameron,
I'll demand an explanation.

172
00:11:16.797 --> 00:11:17.457
You will?

173
00:11:17.537 --> 00:11:18.957
Then speak your piece.

174
00:11:19.037 --> 00:11:21.978
Mr. Thorpe, will you please
take me to my brother?

175
00:11:23.157 --> 00:11:24.457
With pleasure.

176
00:11:25.297 --> 00:11:27.057
I'll be looking for you shortly.

177
00:11:27.137 --> 00:11:29.019
Well, I won't be hard to locate.

178
00:11:39.877 --> 00:11:41.597
Hello, honey girl.

179
00:11:42.897 --> 00:11:45.077
Mr. Sark. Great pleasure.

180
00:11:46.077 --> 00:11:49.717
Just think this wagon will be
your home for the next six months.

181
00:11:49.797 --> 00:11:53.157
And after that, the
cabin in the wilderness.

182
00:11:53.897 --> 00:11:55.617
My mind is made up, Mr.

183
00:11:55.697 --> 00:11:56.297
Sark.

184
00:11:56.377 --> 00:11:58.237
We're going with the settlers.

185
00:12:00.557 --> 00:12:02.197
Howdy, boys! Hello, Dick.

186
00:12:02.277 --> 00:12:03.397
Howdy, Bill.

187
00:12:03.717 --> 00:12:05.037
Hey, Tex.

188
00:12:05.117 --> 00:12:07.397
I didn't tell you about
this here boy Coleman.

189
00:12:07.477 --> 00:12:11.117
He can heave a knife into
a mark so big every time.

190
00:12:11.197 --> 00:12:14.477
I'll bet you, Buffalo,
of he even left postback.

191
00:12:14.557 --> 00:12:15.877
Call the bet.

192
00:12:16.657 --> 00:12:18.717
Now, here, show him, boy.

193
00:12:30.437 --> 00:12:32.437
Bless, now, wild heart.

194
00:12:32.517 --> 00:12:35.317
Oh, I've seen him do it
a hundred times, eh, Bill?

195
00:12:35.397 --> 00:12:37.985
That's another buffalo
hide you owe me, Tex.

196
00:12:38.197 --> 00:12:41.197
You remember, Bill, that
time up on the Snake River?

197
00:12:41.277 --> 00:12:42.657
Oh, boy, Daniel.

198
00:12:42.897 --> 00:12:46.877
Hey, boy, I want to know
about old Ben's grizzles.

199
00:12:47.037 --> 00:12:49.337
I hear the Indians downed him.

200
00:12:49.417 --> 00:12:51.537
Only it wasn't Indians downed him.

201
00:12:51.617 --> 00:12:52.577
How?

202
00:12:52.657 --> 00:12:54.077
Renegade White's done it.

203
00:12:54.157 --> 00:12:55.217
How come?

204
00:12:55.297 --> 00:12:56.937
He'd been wolfing all winter.

205
00:12:57.017 --> 00:12:58.017
Yeah.

206
00:12:58.097 --> 00:13:01.237
Once they had two, three thousand
dollars worth of wolf pelts.

207
00:13:01.317 --> 00:13:02.737
Oh, easy, man.

208
00:13:03.337 --> 00:13:06.177
He was hacked up and stuck full arrow.

209
00:13:06.297 --> 00:13:08.937
It looked like engine work all right.

210
00:13:09.277 --> 00:13:11.457
The wolf pelts was gone.

211
00:13:12.897 --> 00:13:14.597
And there was other things.

212
00:13:14.837 --> 00:13:16.657
Renegade White's done it.

213
00:13:18.277 --> 00:13:22.577
If ever I find them hellhounds,
I'll sure make them hunt their holes.

214
00:13:29.877 --> 00:13:30.997
All right.

215
00:13:38.157 --> 00:13:40.857
Robert, who's that young buck over there?

216
00:13:40.937 --> 00:13:43.097
With no hair on his face.

217
00:13:43.177 --> 00:13:44.177
Him?

218
00:13:44.397 --> 00:13:46.597
That's, uh, bred Cole.

219
00:13:46.777 --> 00:13:48.737
He's very quick with his knife.

220
00:13:48.817 --> 00:13:50.097
Where does he come from?

221
00:13:50.177 --> 00:13:53.597
He come from the plains, the mountains.

222
00:13:53.677 --> 00:13:55.457
He live with the Indians.

223
00:13:55.557 --> 00:13:58.957
He can throw a knife
through the heart at 20 feet.

224
00:13:59.877 --> 00:14:01.157
He's got a shot in this country.

225
00:14:01.237 --> 00:14:02.757
He knows everything.

226
00:14:03.057 --> 00:14:06.337
He'll know too much for
his own good some days.

227
00:14:17.917 --> 00:14:22.637
If old Ben had lived, he'd be
going on about 72 now, wouldn't he?

228
00:14:58.157 --> 00:15:00.357
It was Renegade White.

229
00:15:10.337 --> 00:15:12.757
And they left their mark.

230
00:15:34.557 --> 00:15:37.037
Oh, I say I do.

231
00:15:38.137 --> 00:15:42.017
Say, Zeke, who was that he
grizzly that just went by?

232
00:15:42.097 --> 00:15:44.397
Why, that's Red Flack.
He's bullwhacking for Wellmore.

233
00:15:44.477 --> 00:15:45.737
He's gonna whack Wellmore's thing.

234
00:15:45.817 --> 00:15:46.757
Cheers to the orange.

235
00:15:46.837 --> 00:15:50.297
You reckon you'll ever
find out who downed old Ben?

236
00:15:50.417 --> 00:15:54.777
Just possible that a certain
lowdown coyote left his sign there.

237
00:16:01.577 --> 00:16:03.837
Hello, Coleman. Howdy, Wilmore.

238
00:16:03.917 --> 00:16:07.277
Change my mind. I'll
scout for that bull train.

239
00:16:07.437 --> 00:16:09.957
Well, that's a ray of sunshine.

240
00:16:10.097 --> 00:16:12.497
Take hands before you
change your mind again.

241
00:16:12.577 --> 00:16:15.477
Got a good wagon boss for the trip?

242
00:16:15.557 --> 00:16:16.457
Red Flack.

243
00:16:16.537 --> 00:16:21.337
A burly roughian that can maul the
toughest freighter on the plains into a pulp

244
00:16:21.417 --> 00:16:23.797
without even getting up a sweat.

245
00:16:23.937 --> 00:16:25.357
He can do that, eh?

246
00:16:25.437 --> 00:16:26.297
Flack?

247
00:16:26.377 --> 00:16:27.937
He likes to do it.

248
00:16:28.017 --> 00:16:30.737
But he can manage a bull train, too.

249
00:16:31.557 --> 00:16:32.657
Bravo.

250
00:16:33.037 --> 00:16:34.617
All right, it's that.

251
00:16:34.697 --> 00:16:36.677
Like the you two have met before.

252
00:16:39.357 --> 00:16:40.457
No.

253
00:16:40.717 --> 00:16:42.857
I reckon not.

254
00:16:43.117 --> 00:16:45.257
Coleman's going to scout for the train.

255
00:16:45.337 --> 00:16:49.037
In fact, he understand that in
the dealing with the Indians,

256
00:16:49.117 --> 00:16:50.697
he's to have final say.

257
00:16:50.777 --> 00:16:51.777
Yes?

258
00:16:51.977 --> 00:16:55.777
Who's got final say about
bussing the bull train?

259
00:16:55.857 --> 00:16:58.717
He understands that you're
the boss of the wagon.

260
00:16:58.797 --> 00:17:01.257
Another thing. Another thing.

261
00:17:01.537 --> 00:17:06.377
Am I supposed to witness them
wooden-head pilgrims across the plains?

262
00:17:06.457 --> 00:17:10.137
Well, now, the more that goes along
is better for them and for you,

263
00:17:10.217 --> 00:17:11.877
in case the Indians jump you.

264
00:17:11.957 --> 00:17:13.357
All right.

265
00:17:13.437 --> 00:17:14.977
All right.

266
00:17:16.977 --> 00:17:19.337
Make it clear to him

267
00:17:19.677 --> 00:17:22.077
that I'm wagon bus.

268
00:17:22.157 --> 00:17:24.377
Oh, he understands that, Flack.

269
00:17:27.277 --> 00:17:30.097
He seems to be a right puddy, Flack.

270
00:17:31.897 --> 00:17:34.357
But he's a real wagon, Mark.

271
00:17:35.177 --> 00:17:37.377
Must have done a big trade in wolf pelts.

272
00:17:37.457 --> 00:17:40.037
Yes, we had a big trade with the wolfers.

273
00:17:41.837 --> 00:17:43.717
Flack sell you any of these?

274
00:17:43.797 --> 00:17:44.817
Flack?

275
00:17:44.957 --> 00:17:48.597
Oh, he didn't do any
wolfing last winter, I guess.

276
00:17:49.437 --> 00:17:52.057
What outfit did you get
the biggest bunch from?

277
00:17:52.137 --> 00:17:54.777
A fella named Lopez.
Came in about a month ago.

278
00:17:54.857 --> 00:17:57.517
It's close on to $5,000 worth.

279
00:17:57.837 --> 00:17:59.417
Lopez, eh?

280
00:18:00.637 --> 00:18:02.157
I don't know him.

281
00:18:02.237 --> 00:18:05.057
I signed him up as a
bullwacker on the train.

282
00:18:05.497 --> 00:18:06.797
You did, eh?

283
00:18:09.617 --> 00:18:11.717
I'll be seeing you next year.

284
00:18:11.817 --> 00:18:12.457
All right.

285
00:18:12.537 --> 00:18:14.277
Bring your scout along back with you.

286
00:18:14.357 --> 00:18:15.657
All right. Goodbye.

287
00:18:17.337 --> 00:18:21.877
Yes, sir. This is the first time that any
outfit ever tried to go cleaner across the

288
00:18:21.957 --> 00:18:24.097
Orch. Is that so? Hello.

289
00:18:24.717 --> 00:18:26.517
I'm going to scout for that bull train.

290
00:18:26.597 --> 00:18:27.597
Good.

291
00:18:29.377 --> 00:18:30.677
Oh, Mr. Cameron, this is Mr.

292
00:18:30.757 --> 00:18:31.857
Coleman. Howdy, Mr. Coleman.

293
00:18:31.937 --> 00:18:35.197
How do you do, sir? He can tell you more
about that country you're going to and the

294
00:18:35.277 --> 00:18:37.937
sort of an outfit that you're
to have than anybody I know.

295
00:18:38.017 --> 00:18:38.997
Thank you, sir.

296
00:18:39.077 --> 00:18:42.697
Well, Wendy, throw my war bag in
with yours and Zeke's, will you?

297
00:18:42.777 --> 00:18:45.057
I sure will. Tell Zeke I'm going long.

298
00:18:45.137 --> 00:18:46.077
All right, boy.

299
00:18:46.157 --> 00:18:47.897
Would you mind looking
over our outfit, Mr.

300
00:18:47.977 --> 00:18:49.497
Coleman? Certainly not.

301
00:18:49.577 --> 00:18:50.757
We'll go have a peek at it.

302
00:18:50.837 --> 00:18:53.117
Where is it? Right over there, sir.

303
00:18:54.197 --> 00:18:56.157
Honey, girl, we must
have your history lesson.

304
00:18:56.237 --> 00:18:58.837
Now, how many stars in the flag?

305
00:18:58.917 --> 00:19:01.497
Twenty-six. How many stripes?

306
00:19:01.757 --> 00:19:02.777
Thirteen.

307
00:19:02.957 --> 00:19:05.217
And what do they stand for?

308
00:19:06.457 --> 00:19:10.457
Why, honey girl, now they stand
for the 13 original colonies.

309
00:19:10.637 --> 00:19:11.897
This is our... Now, who...

310
00:19:11.977 --> 00:19:15.497
Now, Mr. Coleman, this is my sister, Ruth.

311
00:19:16.477 --> 00:19:19.777
Honey girl, it isn't safe to be sitting
in a rocking chair when there's certain

312
00:19:19.857 --> 00:19:21.157
people present.

313
00:19:21.577 --> 00:19:24.117
I think you'll find we have everything.

314
00:19:25.417 --> 00:19:29.497
How about guns? I've got a
rifle and a fouling piece.

315
00:19:29.577 --> 00:19:30.917
Plenty of ammunition?

316
00:19:30.997 --> 00:19:31.917
Plenty.

317
00:19:31.997 --> 00:19:33.517
Good, you'll need it.

318
00:19:38.457 --> 00:19:40.097
I don't see any barrels.

319
00:19:40.177 --> 00:19:43.057
A barrel? Yeah, there'll be
long stretches without water.

320
00:19:43.137 --> 00:19:44.137
You'll need a water barrel.

321
00:19:44.217 --> 00:19:46.017
I knew we'd forget something.

322
00:19:46.097 --> 00:19:47.477
I'll go get one.

323
00:19:47.557 --> 00:19:48.557
All right.

324
00:19:51.617 --> 00:19:53.937
What I was aiming to tell you was this.

325
00:19:54.017 --> 00:19:55.957
When I came into the rig...

326
00:19:56.657 --> 00:19:57.797
Oh,

327
00:19:58.177 --> 00:19:59.417
quick work.

328
00:20:04.337 --> 00:20:07.697
Say, it wouldn't be a bad
idea if you took two barrels.

329
00:20:07.777 --> 00:20:09.497
Suppose you go rustle another one.

330
00:20:09.577 --> 00:20:11.077
I'll do that.

331
00:20:12.877 --> 00:20:15.337
When I came romping in
there, Miss Chairman...

332
00:20:15.417 --> 00:20:16.517
How's this?

333
00:20:16.777 --> 00:20:18.597
Oh, fine.

334
00:20:19.277 --> 00:20:22.817
Looks like barrels draw
on trees around here.

335
00:20:27.937 --> 00:20:29.257
Mr. Cameron?

336
00:20:29.637 --> 00:20:32.931
You better tell your sister
to change that pretty dress.

337
00:20:33.597 --> 00:20:35.337
She won't get very far in that.

338
00:20:35.417 --> 00:20:37.117
She ought to put on
some faddle-ling clothes.

339
00:20:37.197 --> 00:20:38.217
Yes, sir.

340
00:20:39.117 --> 00:20:40.417
Have a seat around here.

341
00:20:40.497 --> 00:20:42.037
I like him better than Mr.

342
00:20:42.117 --> 00:20:45.257
Thorpe. We'll finish your
history-nesting, honey girl.

343
00:20:45.337 --> 00:20:47.877
I don't think. I'm going
to watch you anyway.

344
00:20:47.957 --> 00:20:50.310
I'll tell you wouldn't get away from it.

345
00:20:50.577 --> 00:20:51.577
Oh.

346
00:20:52.037 --> 00:20:55.625
Thorpe, get back on the Peansy
Bell and make yourself scared.

347
00:21:01.897 --> 00:21:07.097
I'll be on the Pinsley
Bell when she leaves.

348
00:21:07.237 --> 00:21:08.717
See the job.

349
00:21:14.297 --> 00:21:16.877
That rums for you and me, eh?

350
00:21:26.957 --> 00:21:33.337
Well, if it ain't, Bill
Thorpey, I always thought you

351
00:21:33.417 --> 00:21:35.757
was hung and planted.

352
00:21:36.077 --> 00:21:37.197
Yars best.

353
00:21:37.277 --> 00:21:39.697
No, my time ain't arrived yet, Black.

354
00:21:39.777 --> 00:21:42.217
So it looks as though it
might be drawing close.

355
00:21:42.297 --> 00:21:43.637
How come?

356
00:21:44.057 --> 00:21:48.217
Well, they promised me a hanging bee
if I don't get out on the peasy bell.

357
00:21:48.297 --> 00:21:52.217
The captain promised me a necktie
party if I set foot on the boat.

358
00:21:52.297 --> 00:21:53.897
It's a case of nowhere to go.

359
00:21:53.977 --> 00:21:57.897
Yes, to me, you do your
shooting by daylight, eh?

360
00:21:58.017 --> 00:22:00.577
With too many people looking on.

361
00:22:01.857 --> 00:22:06.417
Well, as long as you can't
go and you can't stay,

362
00:22:06.617 --> 00:22:09.877
just what do you think
you'll do about it, eh?

363
00:22:09.957 --> 00:22:12.217
Well, I've always been able to wiggle out.

364
00:22:12.297 --> 00:22:16.117
Yeah, appears to me as if you
was born to be drowned, eh?

365
00:22:16.197 --> 00:22:17.317
Stop it.

366
00:22:20.097 --> 00:22:21.397
Stop it.

367
00:22:22.497 --> 00:22:26.457
Come on, get rid of that move,
sir, and let's get out of this.

368
00:22:26.537 --> 00:22:28.057
No, it's me, boy.

369
00:22:28.137 --> 00:22:29.317
Get your head up.

370
00:22:29.817 --> 00:22:31.357
Now, it's all, folks.

371
00:22:31.437 --> 00:22:32.857
See you next year.

372
00:22:40.617 --> 00:22:46.057
Are you just as handy
with a gun as you was?

373
00:22:47.217 --> 00:22:49.777
I can drive a nail at 30 feet.

374
00:22:49.857 --> 00:22:50.857
Yes.

375
00:22:51.197 --> 00:22:52.317
Well,

376
00:22:52.797 --> 00:22:58.317
as long as you can't
go and you can't stay,

377
00:22:59.557 --> 00:23:05.657
wouldn't be a bad idea if you was to go
along with me well that sounds reasonable

378
00:23:05.737 --> 00:23:12.017
where do you happen to be headed
for anyways he's out there while

379
00:23:12.097 --> 00:23:15.077
the night nooks noose are waiting for you

380
00:23:17.937 --> 00:23:21.077
There he is, Wendy. I trapped
him down at Joe's with this jug.

381
00:23:21.157 --> 00:23:22.117
Hey, Wendy!

382
00:23:22.197 --> 00:23:26.597
He's the last you see of
civilization for all time.

383
00:23:26.677 --> 00:23:27.677
Hey!

384
00:23:27.837 --> 00:23:29.497
Back up here. Back up.

385
00:23:29.577 --> 00:23:32.957
I want to finish that with Wendy.

386
00:23:33.037 --> 00:23:34.057
Yeah.

387
00:23:35.517 --> 00:23:39.817
That's what you get for
not taking a drink with me.

388
00:23:39.997 --> 00:23:41.877
I'll dance at your next wedding.

389
00:23:41.957 --> 00:23:44.297
You'll drink at my next wedding, not that.

390
00:23:44.377 --> 00:23:46.057
Seth, wait.

391
00:23:46.277 --> 00:23:49.577
Give me one of them things you know.

392
00:23:50.377 --> 00:23:52.377
Nah, that's an old one.

393
00:23:52.617 --> 00:23:54.717
No, no, the coyote.

394
00:23:54.797 --> 00:23:56.657
Oh, well, boy.

395
00:23:56.737 --> 00:23:58.337
And the Indians.

396
00:23:58.837 --> 00:24:00.197
Ah, Seth.

397
00:24:01.897 --> 00:24:04.997
Hey, you killed him a dead Indian?

398
00:24:05.077 --> 00:24:06.657
No, I never killed a dead one.

399
00:24:06.737 --> 00:24:08.502
Before they was dead, did you?

400
00:24:08.777 --> 00:24:11.457
No, you see, the Indians are my friends.

401
00:24:11.757 --> 00:24:14.437
They taught me all I know about the woods.

402
00:24:14.677 --> 00:24:17.957
They taught me how to follow
a trail by watching the leaves.

403
00:24:18.037 --> 00:24:21.837
How to cut your mark on a tree so
you won't get lost in the forest.

404
00:24:21.917 --> 00:24:25.317
And they taught me how to bury in in
the snow so you won't freeze to death in

405
00:24:25.397 --> 00:24:26.397
storms.

406
00:24:26.797 --> 00:24:30.268
And they taught me how to make
a fire without even a flint.

407
00:24:31.637 --> 00:24:34.397
They taught me how to make
the best bow and arrows, too.

408
00:24:34.477 --> 00:24:37.065
Did they teach you how
to make cat poosters?

409
00:24:37.477 --> 00:24:38.477
No,

410
00:24:39.137 --> 00:24:41.019
that's one of their own secrets.

411
00:24:41.317 --> 00:24:43.717
Well, boys, I guess we better get going.

412
00:24:53.717 --> 00:24:56.397
Oh, God, our Father,

413
00:24:56.597 --> 00:25:01.677
as you sit on high and look down on
us poor mortals, forgive our prayers.

414
00:25:02.077 --> 00:25:06.557
I am about to lead these people
into a wild and dangerous country.

415
00:25:06.817 --> 00:25:11.317
Give me strength and wisdom,
oh God, to lead them through.

416
00:25:15.857 --> 00:25:17.557
I'm going to get those big.

417
00:25:17.637 --> 00:25:19.037
Get in. Get in, folks.

418
00:25:19.117 --> 00:25:20.117
We're going.

419
00:25:20.437 --> 00:25:22.557
Well, we're going now. Get in there.

420
00:25:24.977 --> 00:25:26.157
Where's my steps?

421
00:25:26.237 --> 00:25:28.497
Mama, I got everything
packed up in the wagon.

422
00:25:28.577 --> 00:25:30.377
How can I get in the wagon, you idiot?

423
00:25:30.457 --> 00:25:31.757
Well, look. I sure. Look, Mama.

424
00:25:31.837 --> 00:25:33.217
Put your feet up on there.

425
00:25:33.297 --> 00:25:34.697
That's it. Now, wait. A lift.

426
00:25:34.777 --> 00:25:36.257
That's it. Off you go, Mama.

427
00:25:36.337 --> 00:25:38.137
Now, one more foot up. Now, up, Mama.

428
00:25:38.217 --> 00:25:39.557
Up, Mama. That's it.

429
00:25:39.637 --> 00:25:40.477
Great, Mama.

430
00:25:40.557 --> 00:25:42.457
You're sitting on my head, Mama.

431
00:25:42.537 --> 00:25:44.797
Please. That's it. There you go.

432
00:25:51.577 --> 00:25:53.397
Give us a shot.

433
00:26:07.577 --> 00:26:09.897
Never mind. I walked there.

434
00:26:09.977 --> 00:26:11.237
Come on.

435
00:26:14.377 --> 00:26:16.957
Come on.

436
00:26:47.757 --> 00:26:51.097
Come on, little cattle.

437
00:26:51.197 --> 00:26:55.917
Come on, little cattle.

438
00:28:22.817 --> 00:28:24.717
Oh

439
00:28:45.617 --> 00:28:47.097
Get in, George!

440
00:29:01.357 --> 00:29:03.637
Howdy, Dave. Hello, Coleman.

441
00:29:03.717 --> 00:29:05.217
Oh, Miss Cameron.

442
00:29:06.277 --> 00:29:10.037
I'm glad you took my advice
about saving that pretty dress.

443
00:29:11.077 --> 00:29:15.037
If you look so nice in it,
it would be a shame to spoil it.

444
00:29:29.477 --> 00:29:31.817
Looking for anyone particularly?

445
00:29:32.077 --> 00:29:38.057
Honey, girl, a gentleman never comes
to a lady's home when he isn't wanted.

446
00:29:38.137 --> 00:29:41.677
Out here, this wagon is our only home.

447
00:29:42.497 --> 00:29:44.557
Only that means us.

448
00:30:16.257 --> 00:30:18.677
But I'm still mystified, Mr.

449
00:30:18.757 --> 00:30:22.639
Thorpe, why you came here instead
of returning to your plantation.

450
00:30:22.997 --> 00:30:24.917
I've told you why I came.

451
00:30:24.997 --> 00:30:29.277
I induced Captain Hollister, an old
friend of mine, to put back to shore,

452
00:30:29.357 --> 00:30:31.297
and I followed you.

453
00:30:31.497 --> 00:30:35.417
Yes, I know that's what you told me,
but I'm afraid you'll flatter her.

454
00:30:35.497 --> 00:30:36.497
Oh!

455
00:30:46.557 --> 00:30:48.637
Oh, my God.

456
00:31:25.357 --> 00:31:27.357
Oh, my God.

457
00:31:56.357 --> 00:31:58.817
We dance well together, don't you think?

458
00:32:01.517 --> 00:32:02.997
Lovely night.

459
00:32:05.297 --> 00:32:06.737
Lovely girl.

460
00:32:07.297 --> 00:32:09.557
Now's your chance. Now's your chance.

461
00:32:09.637 --> 00:32:12.397
Go in and snag her away from me.

462
00:32:21.217 --> 00:32:23.017
I claim the fame.

463
00:32:32.417 --> 00:32:34.657
Well, Zeke. Oh, boy.

464
00:32:34.737 --> 00:32:37.837
Thorpe just stole my gardener
and let me dance in with myself.

465
00:32:37.917 --> 00:32:38.917
Yeah?

466
00:32:39.357 --> 00:32:40.357
Say, boy.

467
00:32:40.437 --> 00:32:44.597
It just come to me a minute ago
where I seen that bear Thorpe before.

468
00:32:44.677 --> 00:32:45.177
Where?

469
00:32:45.237 --> 00:32:47.977
Camped on the Shimmering
with Flack and Lopez.

470
00:32:48.057 --> 00:32:49.237
Their old friends.

471
00:32:49.317 --> 00:32:51.317
Are you sure of that? Yeah, it's hard.

472
00:32:51.397 --> 00:32:54.017
So keep your eye peeled on him, son.

473
00:32:54.097 --> 00:32:56.897
No, I'm tired. I think
I'll go in my wagon.

474
00:32:56.977 --> 00:32:58.097
Why, certainly.

475
00:32:58.177 --> 00:32:59.677
I'll take you there.

476
00:33:05.417 --> 00:33:10.477
I have to think this same moon is
shining on my old plantation in Louisiana.

477
00:33:19.177 --> 00:33:22.917
All it needs is a lovely
woman to preside there.

478
00:33:22.997 --> 00:33:24.837
Someday you'll find her.

479
00:33:25.357 --> 00:33:27.117
I have found her, Ruth. Please, Mr.

480
00:33:27.197 --> 00:33:29.477
Sork, as I said before,

481
00:33:29.717 --> 00:33:32.117
there can be no happiness without love.

482
00:33:32.197 --> 00:33:33.897
But love will come.

483
00:33:48.637 --> 00:33:49.437
Ruth.

484
00:33:49.517 --> 00:33:50.757
I'm really tired, Mr.

485
00:33:50.837 --> 00:33:53.072
Sork. Do you mind if I say good night?

486
00:33:53.557 --> 00:33:54.817
Good night.

487
00:34:16.217 --> 00:34:19.077
We're getting into
dangerous country, Flack.

488
00:34:19.157 --> 00:34:22.857
So I'll be riding to the Pawnee
villages to pick up some Indian scouts.

489
00:34:22.937 --> 00:34:26.537
Yes, well, you'll likely
lose your scalp out there.

490
00:34:27.617 --> 00:34:31.146
I'll bet you a couple of wolf
pelts I bring it back with me.

491
00:34:34.237 --> 00:34:36.317
How long you begun, Coleman?

492
00:34:37.017 --> 00:34:39.437
Three or four days, a week maybe.

493
00:34:39.517 --> 00:34:41.037
Back so soon.

494
00:34:41.477 --> 00:34:44.477
I thought maybe you wouldn't
be coming back at all.

495
00:34:44.597 --> 00:34:46.577
And just why did you think that?

496
00:34:49.397 --> 00:34:54.217
Well, after I sort of took the
dark-eyed beauty away from you,

497
00:34:54.297 --> 00:34:56.297
I thought you might be decanting.

498
00:34:59.737 --> 00:35:01.217
Listen, Thorpe.

499
00:35:01.917 --> 00:35:04.677
I never quit a job in
the middle of the road.

500
00:35:04.757 --> 00:35:06.777
Oh, quite so, quite so.

501
00:35:06.857 --> 00:35:09.357
But after the girl quit you
in the middle of the road...

502
00:35:09.437 --> 00:35:11.297
Say that again, Mr. Thorpe.

503
00:35:15.197 --> 00:35:17.497
I know who you are now.

504
00:35:17.797 --> 00:35:21.097
And I know why you quit
the Simaran country, too.

505
00:35:23.397 --> 00:35:26.777
Oh, well, no necessity to
have quarrels among friends.

506
00:35:26.857 --> 00:35:27.857
Friends?

507
00:35:28.597 --> 00:35:30.837
You threw too wide a loop.

508
00:35:31.337 --> 00:35:32.517
Remember this.

509
00:35:32.597 --> 00:35:34.197
The three of you.

510
00:35:35.457 --> 00:35:37.237
I'm not your friend.

511
00:35:37.317 --> 00:35:38.493
I'm not your friend.

512
00:35:47.377 --> 00:35:50.177
Well, you let him scare you stiff.

513
00:35:50.377 --> 00:35:51.717
Not at all.

514
00:35:52.077 --> 00:35:56.317
Only an idiot, you know, presses a quarrel
when the other man has a knife pressed

515
00:35:56.397 --> 00:35:57.437
against him.

516
00:35:57.657 --> 00:35:59.157
Good excuse.

517
00:35:59.957 --> 00:36:01.757
Wolf pelt, eh?

518
00:36:02.517 --> 00:36:05.097
What does that mean? Don't mean nothing.

519
00:36:05.177 --> 00:36:07.517
It doesn't to me, but it does to you.

520
00:36:07.597 --> 00:36:09.479
Yeah? Why'd you get that notion?

521
00:36:10.797 --> 00:36:13.326
You look like he had
thrown a knife in you.

522
00:36:13.737 --> 00:36:16.417
Not exactly what I'd call a poker face.

523
00:36:16.497 --> 00:36:18.517
Well, what of it?

524
00:36:19.757 --> 00:36:20.777
Nothing.

525
00:36:21.917 --> 00:36:25.857
Only I'm beginning to
understand why you don't like...

526
00:36:25.937 --> 00:36:26.957
Coleman.

527
00:36:34.997 --> 00:36:36.357
Bye, Wendy.

528
00:36:36.917 --> 00:36:40.357
I'll be seeing you in the
hunting grounds, if not before.

529
00:36:41.797 --> 00:36:42.797
Goodbye.

530
00:36:43.537 --> 00:36:47.557
Well, Miss Ruth, I have
some good news for you.

531
00:36:47.637 --> 00:36:48.637
What?

532
00:36:48.737 --> 00:36:50.997
I'm going to be away for a while.

533
00:36:51.077 --> 00:36:52.337
I'm going to be a scout.

534
00:36:52.417 --> 00:36:55.297
Isn't that dangerous in the open country?

535
00:36:55.537 --> 00:36:56.697
Lord, no.

536
00:36:56.777 --> 00:36:58.217
I love it.

537
00:36:58.457 --> 00:37:02.597
Especially now that it's spring
and everything is so happy.

538
00:37:03.077 --> 00:37:09.377
Why, these trees out there, big tall
pines, just a reachin' and a reachin',

539
00:37:09.457 --> 00:37:13.017
As if they wanted to climb right
through the gates of heaven.

540
00:37:13.097 --> 00:37:14.757
And there's Brooks, too,

541
00:37:14.997 --> 00:37:17.617
with the water smiling all day long.

542
00:37:18.197 --> 00:37:21.097
But the part I like best is the night.

543
00:37:21.877 --> 00:37:27.737
Lying out there beneath a blanket of stars,
with that old moon smiling down on you.

544
00:37:28.437 --> 00:37:32.097
And every time you look up, there she is.

545
00:37:32.177 --> 00:37:36.397
Sort of guarding over you,
like a mother minding her young.

546
00:37:38.657 --> 00:37:43.217
Sometimes it's so beautiful
that I just lie there, listening.

547
00:37:44.017 --> 00:37:45.457
Birds singing,

548
00:37:46.237 --> 00:37:48.017
brooks laughing,

549
00:37:49.017 --> 00:37:54.477
and the wind sort of crooning through
the forest, like some great orc.

550
00:37:55.557 --> 00:37:57.957
Oh, I've always loved it.

551
00:38:00.097 --> 00:38:03.377
But I reckon I'm going
to be lonely this time.

552
00:38:04.997 --> 00:38:09.557
You know, you can get sort of used
to having somebody not like you.

553
00:38:11.057 --> 00:38:14.037
When they're not around, you miss them.

554
00:38:14.477 --> 00:38:16.097
Not liking you.

555
00:38:17.177 --> 00:38:19.824
That's why I reckon I'm
going to be lonesome.

556
00:38:21.537 --> 00:38:23.537
But I'll be thinking of you.

557
00:38:24.777 --> 00:38:25.797
Goodbye.

558
00:38:29.317 --> 00:38:32.797
And you just take care
you don't lose your scalp.

559
00:38:32.877 --> 00:38:34.457
Is he leaving the train?

560
00:38:34.537 --> 00:38:37.017
Yes, miss. He's riding
out to Pawnee villages.

561
00:38:37.097 --> 00:38:38.537
Well, how far are they?

562
00:38:38.617 --> 00:38:40.857
Oh, nigh on a hundred miles.

563
00:38:41.237 --> 00:38:42.657
Wasn't that dangerous?

564
00:38:42.737 --> 00:38:46.037
Well, he's likely to lose his
scalp before he gets there.

565
00:38:46.117 --> 00:38:48.257
But once in the villages, he's safe.

566
00:38:48.337 --> 00:38:51.117
So don't you worry about him, miss.

567
00:38:52.037 --> 00:38:53.997
Why should I worry about him?

568
00:38:54.077 --> 00:38:55.957
I don't know, miss. I don't know.

569
00:38:56.037 --> 00:38:58.657
But it seemed like as if maybe you was.

570
00:38:58.737 --> 00:39:00.697
Not at all. He means nothing to me.

571
00:39:00.777 --> 00:39:02.797
No. No, of course not.

572
00:39:02.877 --> 00:39:04.217
Good night.

573
00:39:04.777 --> 00:39:06.637
Good night, Pete.

574
00:39:37.437 --> 00:39:39.957
Well, you got back here at last, eh?

575
00:39:40.037 --> 00:39:41.037
Yeah.

576
00:39:41.457 --> 00:39:43.937
Many of Buffalo signs out here.

577
00:39:44.237 --> 00:39:47.017
So I'll be riding out to get
fresh meat for the outfit.

578
00:39:47.097 --> 00:39:48.417
Well, who's keeping you?

579
00:39:48.497 --> 00:39:50.877
I'll be seeing you at the river cross.

580
00:39:56.417 --> 00:39:58.197
Hey, Lopez!

581
00:39:58.337 --> 00:40:00.337
Lopez, up!

582
00:40:00.717 --> 00:40:01.717
Here.

583
00:40:02.677 --> 00:40:03.677
Here.

584
00:40:06.457 --> 00:40:09.297
You two have been waiting for your chance.

585
00:40:09.377 --> 00:40:10.797
Here it is.

586
00:40:10.877 --> 00:40:13.777
Go out on a buffalo hunt.

587
00:40:13.857 --> 00:40:14.737
Me?

588
00:40:14.817 --> 00:40:17.197
I kill hundreds of buffalo.

589
00:40:17.277 --> 00:40:21.157
Where should I go? Get them
cobwebs out of your brain.

590
00:40:21.517 --> 00:40:24.977
He means, Lopez, we'll find that again.

591
00:40:47.077 --> 00:40:48.857
Watch him till he leaves.

592
00:40:48.937 --> 00:40:51.677
The ponies are there in the back.

593
00:41:04.437 --> 00:41:05.437
Thank you.

594
00:43:00.797 --> 00:43:02.017
Hey!

595
00:43:02.217 --> 00:43:04.337
Hey! You pilgrims! Come here!

596
00:43:04.417 --> 00:43:05.477
Come here! Yeah,

597
00:43:05.717 --> 00:43:06.717
Bascom?

598
00:43:06.837 --> 00:43:08.537
Yes. Bascom? Yes.

599
00:43:08.617 --> 00:43:12.517
I'll shove the horses and
the cattle right on through.

600
00:43:12.597 --> 00:43:15.757
Leave them wheelers hooked to them wagons.

601
00:43:15.837 --> 00:43:21.857
Well, once you take to the water, well,
it's every man and critter for his self,

602
00:43:21.937 --> 00:43:22.937
eh?

603
00:43:23.157 --> 00:43:24.457
Get out of here.

604
00:43:24.537 --> 00:43:25.777
Get out of here. Good.

605
00:43:25.857 --> 00:43:26.857
Mr. Fletch.

606
00:43:27.337 --> 00:43:29.977
How can I get my mule uses across?

607
00:43:30.057 --> 00:43:33.457
Well, get your mother-in-law
to ride him, eh?

608
00:43:34.877 --> 00:43:35.397
Yes?

609
00:43:35.477 --> 00:43:38.477
Mr. Bascom, you know,
I don't like that fella.

610
00:43:38.557 --> 00:43:42.237
No? He's the kind who will pat you on your
back to your face and then laugh in your

611
00:43:42.317 --> 00:43:44.937
face behind your back. And another thing.

612
00:43:45.017 --> 00:43:49.097
Yes? If he had a mother-in-law
like mine, he would never laugh.

613
00:43:57.877 --> 00:43:59.897
The hunt was a great success.

614
00:43:59.977 --> 00:44:01.857
We bagged our buffalo.

615
00:44:01.997 --> 00:44:03.437
You got your meat.

616
00:44:03.517 --> 00:44:04.517
Eh?

617
00:44:05.257 --> 00:44:08.057
This is the best shot I've ever seen.

618
00:44:08.577 --> 00:44:09.677
Well,

619
00:44:10.597 --> 00:44:12.277
we better be shoving off.

620
00:45:11.537 --> 00:45:15.437
Oh, my God.

621
00:46:55.737 --> 00:46:57.937
I see you took a bath.

622
00:46:58.737 --> 00:47:00.277
Yes, yes.

623
00:47:01.217 --> 00:47:03.897
You got a slug of whiskey.

624
00:47:03.977 --> 00:47:05.537
No, I left my jug.

625
00:47:05.617 --> 00:47:07.797
I hid it in the Cameron's wagon.

626
00:47:08.537 --> 00:47:10.577
By the way, where is my little beauty?

627
00:47:10.657 --> 00:47:14.137
Well, she's, she's somewhere around.

628
00:47:14.357 --> 00:47:17.677
Well, now that you've
got her all to yourself,

629
00:47:18.017 --> 00:47:19.697
What do you have to do with that?

630
00:47:19.777 --> 00:47:23.157
I think I'll take her back
and settle on my plantation.

631
00:47:23.237 --> 00:47:26.517
Your plantation, eh?

632
00:47:28.137 --> 00:47:33.697
Lopez, he's hollered so much
about that's how plantation he is.

633
00:47:33.777 --> 00:47:35.917
He believes it himself, eh?

634
00:47:36.777 --> 00:47:37.557
What?

635
00:47:37.637 --> 00:47:40.337
Did your thought we had no plantation?

636
00:47:40.837 --> 00:47:42.337
Plantation, eh?

637
00:47:42.417 --> 00:47:46.977
All you got in the world
is a dirty dick of cars

638
00:47:49.097 --> 00:47:51.617
Yeah, Corbin's been gone two days.

639
00:47:51.697 --> 00:47:54.638
Yeah, I've been kind of
worried about that myself.

640
00:48:03.437 --> 00:48:07.496
Eagle Cave says last time he's seen
him, he was headed for the train.

641
00:48:07.717 --> 00:48:10.737
Another thing, the Camerons
haven't crossed yet.

642
00:48:10.817 --> 00:48:14.077
No, I'd better start around down
there and see what's holding them.

643
00:48:14.157 --> 00:48:16.237
Yes, we'd better help them across.

644
00:48:22.217 --> 00:48:24.197
Well, I think we can...

645
00:48:24.277 --> 00:48:27.057
We were just wondering
what it's become of you.

646
00:48:27.137 --> 00:48:31.497
Where's your horse? He stepped in a
prairie dog hole and broke his neck.

647
00:48:31.917 --> 00:48:33.457
Come near breaking mine, too.

648
00:48:33.537 --> 00:48:34.537
Are you hurt?

649
00:48:34.777 --> 00:48:37.417
No, I was knocked out for a spell.

650
00:48:37.817 --> 00:48:40.877
Here, I'll put these in your
wagon and help you across.

651
00:48:40.957 --> 00:48:43.637
Slack said we could only use the wheelers.

652
00:48:43.717 --> 00:48:44.957
Slack said?

653
00:48:45.037 --> 00:48:47.097
What does he know about water?

654
00:48:56.257 --> 00:48:57.577
All right, boys.

655
00:48:57.657 --> 00:48:58.657
Johnny!

656
00:49:05.657 --> 00:49:07.937
There's the Cameron wagon now.

657
00:49:14.117 --> 00:49:16.037
I'll go greet the little filly.

658
00:49:16.117 --> 00:49:17.317
Greet, eh?

659
00:49:18.157 --> 00:49:21.197
me go greet the jug, eh?

660
00:49:21.277 --> 00:49:23.017
Ah, the world was it.

661
00:49:27.757 --> 00:49:30.177
You take them from here on in, Dave.

662
00:49:30.257 --> 00:49:31.297
Shallow water.

663
00:49:31.377 --> 00:49:32.837
All right, Dave. I'll
back and get my saddle.

664
00:49:32.917 --> 00:49:33.917
All right.

665
00:49:37.257 --> 00:49:39.357
Get up. Come on, Shorty.

666
00:49:39.437 --> 00:49:40.557
Get up.

667
00:49:57.237 --> 00:49:59.137
I was just coming over to help you.

668
00:49:59.217 --> 00:50:01.537
Thank you. We had the best of help.

669
00:50:01.617 --> 00:50:02.357
Help?

670
00:50:02.437 --> 00:50:03.437
Who?

671
00:50:08.317 --> 00:50:10.697
The matter, Lopez? Seeing a few ghosts?

672
00:50:10.777 --> 00:50:12.437
Me? No. No.

673
00:50:18.417 --> 00:50:20.537
Drive on into the corral, Dave.

674
00:50:20.617 --> 00:50:21.517
All right.

675
00:50:21.597 --> 00:50:22.437
Get in.

676
00:50:22.517 --> 00:50:23.797
Come on in.

677
00:50:23.877 --> 00:50:24.997
Get up there.

678
00:50:25.937 --> 00:50:29.457
I'll be seeing you three
later about matters and things.

679
00:50:38.977 --> 00:50:41.517
Hello, boy. Howdy, Zeke.

680
00:50:41.597 --> 00:50:42.857
What happened?

681
00:50:42.937 --> 00:50:44.757
Pony stepped in a dog hole.

682
00:50:44.837 --> 00:50:48.637
Yeah? I suppose a prairie dog shot that
hole through your saddle and into your

683
00:50:48.717 --> 00:50:49.717
horse.

684
00:50:50.657 --> 00:50:51.777
Thank you.

685
00:51:02.437 --> 00:51:04.817
Who was going from camp, Zeke?

686
00:51:05.437 --> 00:51:07.837
Thorpe and Lopez come in during the night.

687
00:51:07.917 --> 00:51:10.976
In the early morning,
sent a wagon out for the meat.

688
00:51:13.517 --> 00:51:17.577
Oh, you made a nice mess of it.

689
00:51:17.657 --> 00:51:18.857
Not at all.

690
00:51:20.277 --> 00:51:24.357
Remember, 200 yards running
is considerable of a handicap.

691
00:51:24.817 --> 00:51:25.917
Besides,

692
00:51:26.497 --> 00:51:28.497
there are other days coming.

693
00:51:28.577 --> 00:51:30.977
Well, don't you fool yourself.

694
00:51:31.057 --> 00:51:32.677
Here he is. Here he is.

695
00:51:33.817 --> 00:51:34.917
Black,

696
00:51:35.117 --> 00:51:38.277
the engine's been sending up
smoke signals for several days.

697
00:51:38.357 --> 00:51:40.317
Yes, well, I see them.

698
00:51:40.617 --> 00:51:43.417
I'll skirmish around with
the Pawnees for a few miles.

699
00:51:43.497 --> 00:51:45.897
Well, go on. There
ain't no one keeping you.

700
00:51:45.977 --> 00:51:49.457
No, but you'd better keep
Thorpe and Lopez here.

701
00:51:49.537 --> 00:51:50.537
Why?

702
00:51:51.117 --> 00:51:55.077
I got a feeling that if
either one of them leaves camp,

703
00:51:56.317 --> 00:51:58.177
they'll never come back.

704
00:51:58.257 --> 00:51:59.917
What do you mean by that?

705
00:52:00.097 --> 00:52:01.757
Just the way it sounded.

706
00:52:01.837 --> 00:52:04.157
Hey, look now. Look now, eh?

707
00:52:05.977 --> 00:52:06.997
Engine?

708
00:52:08.557 --> 00:52:09.557
What?

709
00:52:15.617 --> 00:52:16.617
Indians?

710
00:52:16.777 --> 00:52:18.317
Why, they're on to it.

711
00:52:18.397 --> 00:52:20.257
Every man to his post.

712
00:52:20.557 --> 00:52:21.557
No fire.

713
00:52:21.657 --> 00:52:23.297
Try a long shot at them.

714
00:52:23.377 --> 00:52:24.717
No fire.

715
00:52:31.117 --> 00:52:32.217
They're Cheyenne.

716
00:52:32.297 --> 00:52:36.137
They want a palaver. They look
to me as if they're out for half.

717
00:52:36.217 --> 00:52:38.511
They will be if we take a shot at them.

718
00:52:38.877 --> 00:52:41.857
That'll mean war. I'll
go on to falaver with him.

719
00:52:49.937 --> 00:52:51.937
Look how clearly his horse is acting.

720
00:52:52.017 --> 00:52:53.817
Yeah, he's riding zigzag.

721
00:52:53.897 --> 00:52:56.917
That's Indian sign that
he wants to falaver.

722
00:53:00.977 --> 00:53:01.977
See?

723
00:53:02.197 --> 00:53:05.717
There's a chief riding out
to meet him now for a powwow.

724
00:53:14.877 --> 00:53:17.697
You're right.

725
00:53:17.777 --> 00:53:19.057
You're right.

726
00:53:27.857 --> 00:53:29.057
What are you doing?

727
00:53:30.097 --> 00:53:31.317
Yes.

728
00:53:32.357 --> 00:53:33.877
Yes.

729
00:53:35.857 --> 00:53:37.777
Let's go.

730
00:53:37.857 --> 00:53:39.677
The war is over there.

731
00:53:41.017 --> 00:53:42.017
Zeke!

732
00:53:42.617 --> 00:53:43.617
Vascom!

733
00:53:51.377 --> 00:53:53.317
I'm not sure what you're doing.

734
00:53:53.397 --> 00:53:55.221
I'm not sure what you're doing.

735
00:53:55.477 --> 00:53:57.817
This is Black Elk, an old friend of mine.

736
00:53:57.897 --> 00:54:00.737
I know that. Do they mean peace or war?

737
00:54:00.817 --> 00:54:04.137
Peace, as long as we march straight through
the Cheyenne country without stopping to

738
00:54:04.217 --> 00:54:05.217
settle.

739
00:54:29.517 --> 00:54:33.517
Now that we're going to be friends,
they'll probably bring their families over here

740
00:54:33.597 --> 00:54:34.517
to beg.

741
00:54:34.597 --> 00:54:38.097
So feed them well and feed them
right, and we'll have no trouble.

742
00:54:38.177 --> 00:54:39.257
All right.

743
00:55:16.257 --> 00:55:19.557
Thank you.

744
00:55:22.597 --> 00:55:24.057
Come on.

745
00:55:44.677 --> 00:55:47.697
Miss Ruth, you shouldn't be
riding out here alone like this,

746
00:55:47.777 --> 00:55:49.877
away from the train. Why not?

747
00:55:50.037 --> 00:55:53.677
Because this is dangerous
country and anything might happen.

748
00:55:53.957 --> 00:55:55.757
You wouldn't care.

749
00:55:55.877 --> 00:55:57.597
Care? Me?

750
00:55:57.677 --> 00:55:59.577
Why should you care?

751
00:55:59.657 --> 00:56:00.977
Listen, girl.

752
00:56:01.057 --> 00:56:05.292
If anything happened to you, it'd be
like throwing my heart to the wall.

753
00:56:07.157 --> 00:56:10.197
Don't worry, it's Black
Yawkin, some of his brave.

754
00:56:14.497 --> 00:56:16.357
It's Coleman Squaw.

755
00:56:16.437 --> 00:56:17.777
Coleman Squaw.

756
00:56:17.857 --> 00:56:20.033
Well, he's saying that I'm your flaw.

757
00:56:20.357 --> 00:56:22.197
Seems like that's what he's driving at.

758
00:56:22.277 --> 00:56:24.557
Well, you tell him that you
don't want me for your flaw.

759
00:56:24.637 --> 00:56:26.997
I've never told Black Elk a lie yet.

760
00:56:27.077 --> 00:56:29.237
He knows my tongue is straight.

761
00:56:29.437 --> 00:56:31.157
What do you mean?

762
00:56:31.237 --> 00:56:34.037
Well, it wouldn't be true if
I told him I didn't want you.

763
00:56:34.117 --> 00:56:35.777
It happens I do.

764
00:56:36.417 --> 00:56:40.711
And you've no better taste than to
tell me that before all these savages?

765
00:56:40.897 --> 00:56:43.603
I'd tell you that in
front of the whole world.

766
00:56:43.817 --> 00:56:46.497
This silly joke has gone far enough.

767
00:57:11.217 --> 00:57:12.757
Thank you.

768
00:58:09.137 --> 00:58:11.037
Help, help, help, please.

769
00:58:23.717 --> 00:58:25.397
All right, first watch.

770
00:58:37.877 --> 00:58:39.677
All right. Hold on.

771
00:58:39.757 --> 00:58:40.717
You're all right.

772
00:58:40.797 --> 00:58:42.417
All right. You're all right.

773
00:58:42.497 --> 00:58:43.837
You're sure you're not.

774
00:58:43.917 --> 00:58:45.337
You'll be fine.

775
00:58:45.897 --> 00:58:47.477
Come on, boy.

776
00:59:19.837 --> 00:59:22.237
Come on. Here, Dave.

777
00:59:22.317 --> 00:59:23.757
Take money, girls.

778
00:59:23.837 --> 00:59:26.237
It's a little easier
going from here on down.

779
00:59:26.317 --> 00:59:29.357
All right, Dave. Now you
cling on to me, Miss Ruth.

780
00:59:32.377 --> 00:59:34.557
Just a little tighter.

781
01:00:01.097 --> 01:00:02.117
Give it to me.

782
01:00:03.157 --> 01:00:04.617
Give it to me.

783
01:00:09.677 --> 01:00:11.737
Are you all right, sonny girl?

784
01:00:12.957 --> 01:00:15.677
It was a pretty bad
place, wasn't it, Beck?

785
01:00:15.757 --> 01:00:18.297
Yeah, but I sort of liked it.

786
01:00:19.077 --> 01:00:21.577
David, let's keep our
wagons down here, Tom.

787
01:00:21.657 --> 01:00:23.077
Thank you, Beck.

788
01:00:25.877 --> 01:00:28.077
Well, well, well, well.

789
01:00:28.157 --> 01:00:33.617
Ha, ha! So I've seen that girl
with her arms around your naked rat.

790
01:00:34.457 --> 01:00:38.057
Yeah, but she sure unwrapped
him when she got on safe footing.

791
01:00:38.137 --> 01:00:39.137
Yeah.

792
01:00:39.777 --> 01:00:42.637
You know, she don't
care nothing about me, Z.

793
01:00:42.717 --> 01:00:46.777
Man, you can never tell how a
woman feels by the way she acts.

794
01:00:47.057 --> 01:00:48.697
They're all riddles, all of them.

795
01:00:48.777 --> 01:00:50.637
And you just gotta guess them.

796
01:00:50.717 --> 01:00:53.657
And no matter which way
you guess, you're wrong.

797
01:00:58.397 --> 01:01:01.777
Looks like as if the way they're
putting some of them outfits over there,

798
01:01:01.857 --> 01:01:03.445
they're going to lose them.

799
01:01:09.737 --> 01:01:10.837
Ha-ha!

800
01:01:10.917 --> 01:01:12.257
What did I tell you?

801
01:01:12.337 --> 01:01:15.337
Let's get out of here
before they get a beat on us.

802
01:01:18.337 --> 01:01:20.557
Zeke, did you hear that terrible crash?

803
01:01:20.637 --> 01:01:22.777
Hear it? I seen it.

804
01:01:23.177 --> 01:01:24.557
Your wife.

805
01:01:24.717 --> 01:01:26.437
Was my mother-in-law in it?

806
01:01:26.517 --> 01:01:29.317
No, she wasn't. Oh, that's too bad.

807
01:01:29.397 --> 01:01:31.977
What'd you say? I said I am glad.

808
01:01:32.077 --> 01:01:35.357
Ah, it's lucky for you that
I wasn't, you laughing hound.

809
01:01:35.437 --> 01:01:36.417
What you mean?

810
01:01:36.497 --> 01:01:39.557
Because I was with your wife,
Sarah, and she gave birth to twins.

811
01:01:39.637 --> 01:01:40.377
Twins?

812
01:01:40.457 --> 01:01:41.957
Are they both mine? Both?

813
01:01:42.037 --> 01:01:43.857
Oh, Mama, are they boys or girls?

814
01:01:43.937 --> 01:01:45.497
One of each? Oh, they.

815
01:01:45.577 --> 01:01:46.737
They're my papa.

816
01:01:47.097 --> 01:01:49.277
Mama, they're my papa.
Papa, they're my mama.

817
01:01:49.357 --> 01:01:51.117
Oh, yeah. I got two for one.

818
01:01:51.197 --> 01:01:52.197
Yeah.

819
01:01:53.157 --> 01:01:57.097
event there's a minute there was two events
they have two drinks here give me that

820
01:01:57.177 --> 01:01:59.737
jug i'll take a pull at that myself

821
01:02:53.277 --> 01:02:55.017
Come on,

822
01:02:55.257 --> 01:02:55.757
Bob.

823
01:02:55.737 --> 01:02:56.777
Come on.

824
01:02:56.857 --> 01:02:57.857
Come on.

825
01:03:20.577 --> 01:03:23.517
Oh, don't touch on a cellar, you home.

826
01:03:23.597 --> 01:03:25.377
It's no use, man.

827
01:03:26.277 --> 01:03:27.937
She's all dried up.

828
01:03:28.017 --> 01:03:32.457
A damned settler is dying off like rats.

829
01:03:32.737 --> 01:03:34.497
We're for moving on.

830
01:03:34.617 --> 01:03:36.277
Come on, Lopez.

831
01:03:36.397 --> 01:03:37.417
Why?

832
01:03:37.617 --> 01:03:40.777
They scattered back all across the desert.

833
01:03:40.937 --> 01:03:44.097
We've got to gather them
up and shut them along.

834
01:03:47.037 --> 01:03:51.217
They say it's not our top, our can
hurt, and it's good by your host.

835
01:04:13.057 --> 01:04:15.717
Old Charlie died, Coleman.

836
01:04:16.197 --> 01:04:18.217
We raised him from a cold.

837
01:04:18.917 --> 01:04:20.177
Talk, boy.

838
01:04:21.077 --> 01:04:22.997
We got to battle it through.

839
01:04:34.097 --> 01:04:36.697
Thank you.

840
01:05:31.437 --> 01:05:33.657
Well, who'd have guessed it?

841
01:05:33.737 --> 01:05:35.577
If it ain't Brett Coleman.

842
01:05:35.657 --> 01:05:36.497
Howdy, Jim.

843
01:05:36.577 --> 01:05:38.317
Where'd you blow in from, boy?

844
01:05:38.397 --> 01:05:40.221
All the way from the big river.

845
01:05:40.857 --> 01:05:44.017
We'd all like to know how
long you're going to camp here.

846
01:05:44.097 --> 01:05:47.337
Well, just as long as it
takes to fix up the outfit.

847
01:06:29.517 --> 01:06:33.357
I've been talking with some trappers
who've just come from the southwest.

848
01:06:33.437 --> 01:06:37.677
They say the country they
call California is wonderful.

849
01:06:37.757 --> 01:06:39.277
Yes, so I've heard.

850
01:06:40.217 --> 01:06:42.737
Why won't you come with
me to a land like that?

851
01:06:42.817 --> 01:06:44.337
Are you going there?

852
01:06:44.417 --> 01:06:46.157
If you'll come with me.

853
01:06:46.377 --> 01:06:49.257
But what about your
plantations in Louisiana?

854
01:06:52.717 --> 01:06:55.717
Well, if we like California better,

855
01:06:56.077 --> 01:07:00.137
we could sell my holdings
and buy vast lands out there.

856
01:07:03.277 --> 01:07:08.217
It's a compliment to offer
me all that, but it can't be.

857
01:07:08.497 --> 01:07:10.057
I'm going to join Daisy.

858
01:07:11.857 --> 01:07:15.797
Oh, Dave, Dave, come over here.

859
01:07:16.377 --> 01:07:21.297
Black Elk here says that you and your
sister were so good to him when he came in to

860
01:07:21.377 --> 01:07:24.957
visit, and now he wants to
give you all them there ponies.

861
01:07:25.037 --> 01:07:29.097
Oh, that's kind of them, Zeke,
but we couldn't take their horses.

862
01:07:29.177 --> 01:07:32.277
Of course you could.
They got hundreds of ponies.

863
01:07:37.977 --> 01:07:40.377
He wants you to show
them where to put them.

864
01:07:40.457 --> 01:07:43.657
Now you go and throw them
ponies into your herd.

865
01:07:43.957 --> 01:07:49.737
Well, Zeke, you lying old coot, that
engine's buying Cameron's sister for

866
01:07:49.817 --> 01:07:51.457
Coleman's squaw.

867
01:07:54.837 --> 01:07:56.737
Well, what about it?

868
01:07:56.817 --> 01:08:00.397
Oh, Coleman's buying himself a squaw, eh?

869
01:08:00.477 --> 01:08:03.417
Zeke, you old whiskered cupid, you.

870
01:08:07.197 --> 01:08:09.937
I loathe the very sight of you.

871
01:08:10.017 --> 01:08:11.877
What have I done now?

872
01:08:13.157 --> 01:08:13.917
Me?

873
01:08:13.997 --> 01:08:17.557
Who else tried to buy
me like an Indian squaw?

874
01:08:17.637 --> 01:08:19.757
You put me to shame before them all.

875
01:08:19.837 --> 01:08:21.897
My girl, you're imagining things.

876
01:08:30.337 --> 01:08:33.637
Zeke always told me women were damn funny.

877
01:08:35.617 --> 01:08:37.197
I've changed my mind.

878
01:08:37.277 --> 01:08:40.097
I will go with you to
California if you'll go at once.

879
01:08:40.177 --> 01:08:41.177
Once?

880
01:08:42.397 --> 01:08:43.997
Why, yes, yes.

881
01:08:45.057 --> 01:08:47.116
I'll make preparations immediately.

882
01:08:48.357 --> 01:08:50.657
This is a fine state of affairs.

883
01:08:51.117 --> 01:08:53.577
This man Thorpe isn't all he claims to be.

884
01:08:53.657 --> 01:08:55.997
You'll find that out.
My mind is made up, Davey.

885
01:08:56.077 --> 01:08:57.606
We're going to California.

886
01:08:59.517 --> 01:09:00.777
Where is class?

887
01:09:11.177 --> 01:09:12.277
Hey!

888
01:09:17.857 --> 01:09:20.097
I just came in to tell you goodbye.

889
01:09:20.177 --> 01:09:21.277
Goodbye?

890
01:09:21.977 --> 01:09:23.797
Where are you going?

891
01:09:24.297 --> 01:09:26.797
I'm going to take my
outfit and leave you here.

892
01:09:26.877 --> 01:09:28.257
Your outfit?

893
01:09:28.337 --> 01:09:32.217
All you got is one horse and two guns.

894
01:09:32.297 --> 01:09:33.077
No.

895
01:09:33.157 --> 01:09:34.897
The Cameron outfit's mine now.

896
01:09:34.977 --> 01:09:36.957
Oh, it is, eh?

897
01:09:37.097 --> 01:09:38.057
Yes.

898
01:09:38.137 --> 01:09:40.037
We're going to California.

899
01:09:40.677 --> 01:09:42.717
I'll bid you a fond farewell.

900
01:09:43.037 --> 01:09:44.557
No, you ain't.

901
01:09:44.977 --> 01:09:46.737
No? No.

902
01:09:47.397 --> 01:09:51.717
Why do you suppose I
grub-stake you for it?

903
01:09:51.797 --> 01:09:54.357
So far, you've been a fizzle.

904
01:09:54.437 --> 01:09:57.097
One try, one miss.

905
01:09:57.177 --> 01:09:58.757
Oh, he's no longer in my way.

906
01:09:58.837 --> 01:10:00.657
Well, he's in mine.

907
01:10:00.737 --> 01:10:02.057
Well, tear him down yourself.

908
01:10:02.137 --> 01:10:05.037
Oh, I could kick him into pulp.

909
01:10:05.117 --> 01:10:08.837
I could break him in two, like that.

910
01:10:09.017 --> 01:10:10.597
Well, why not?

911
01:10:10.677 --> 01:10:11.557
Well,

912
01:10:11.637 --> 01:10:16.877
I don't mind a fist or feet or even a gun.

913
01:10:17.097 --> 01:10:20.757
But it's the way he handles that mess.

914
01:10:20.837 --> 01:10:22.197
Why should I risk it?

915
01:10:22.277 --> 01:10:24.917
Because you're a dead shot.

916
01:10:24.997 --> 01:10:28.557
Flop, you're going to stink.

917
01:10:28.637 --> 01:10:34.337
And you're going to prove how
good you are before you leave.

918
01:10:35.737 --> 01:10:37.257
Howdy, Henry.

919
01:10:38.077 --> 01:10:39.517
How are things, Coleman?

920
01:10:39.597 --> 01:10:40.717
Just fine.

921
01:10:40.877 --> 01:10:41.877
Say,

922
01:10:42.117 --> 01:10:45.497
Black Elk was telling me that all the
Indians to the west were together to keep you

923
01:10:45.577 --> 01:10:47.157
all from passing through.

924
01:10:47.237 --> 01:10:48.637
So they tell me.

925
01:10:49.737 --> 01:10:52.277
Black Elk and the
Cheyennes are going west.

926
01:10:52.357 --> 01:10:54.437
Old Pow Wow is the Shoshone.

927
01:10:55.017 --> 01:10:58.757
Yeah, Black Elk tells me that it's almost
certain that the Cheyennes will declare

928
01:10:58.837 --> 01:10:59.937
war later.

929
01:11:00.077 --> 01:11:01.077
Likely.

930
01:11:01.217 --> 01:11:03.657
Old Pete Rubidoux was
asking about you a while ago.

931
01:11:03.737 --> 01:11:05.137
Pete? Where is he?

932
01:11:05.217 --> 01:11:07.877
Camp Spring Yonder with his new squaw.

933
01:11:07.957 --> 01:11:10.257
I think I'll ramble down and see him.

934
01:11:10.677 --> 01:11:13.577
Say, Henry, will you put a
new cap nipple on this gun?

935
01:11:13.657 --> 01:11:15.117
Sure will, boy.

936
01:11:15.437 --> 01:11:18.297
A new trigger spring in the pistol.

937
01:11:18.377 --> 01:11:19.057
All right.

938
01:11:19.137 --> 01:11:21.157
I'll leave him with
you while I go see Pete.

939
01:11:21.237 --> 01:11:22.884
Be ready when you come back.

940
01:12:01.437 --> 01:12:08.317
We are about to unite this loving and
devoted couple in the holy bonds of wedlock.

941
01:12:12.857 --> 01:12:14.637
I do.

942
01:12:14.797 --> 01:12:20.837
Abigail Vance, do you take this man
to be your lawful wedded husband?

943
01:12:23.177 --> 01:12:24.857
She does.

944
01:12:58.297 --> 01:12:59.877
Thank you.

945
01:13:38.197 --> 01:13:39.737
Oh, no.

946
01:13:40.717 --> 01:13:42.257
Hey, Flack.

947
01:13:43.257 --> 01:13:48.657
You'll recollect as how Coleman done
told you that if Lopez here or Thorpe done

948
01:13:48.737 --> 01:13:51.237
straight off into the brush,
they weren't like this.

949
01:13:51.317 --> 01:13:55.317
I'll never come back. Sure,
he made some kind of a bluff.

950
01:13:55.397 --> 01:13:56.417
What of it?

951
01:13:56.497 --> 01:14:01.117
Well, Thorpe strayed out, and
he ain't a-never coming back.

952
01:14:01.197 --> 01:14:01.977
Honey?

953
01:14:02.057 --> 01:14:03.057
No.

954
01:14:04.577 --> 01:14:07.757
He's done gone back to his old plantation.

955
01:14:08.117 --> 01:14:09.117
Yeah.

956
01:14:14.157 --> 01:14:17.477
Well, you won't go to
California with Thorpe now.

957
01:14:17.557 --> 01:14:18.557
Why not?

958
01:14:19.277 --> 01:14:23.417
He and Coleman just met in
the brush and Coleman shot him.

959
01:14:23.737 --> 01:14:25.217
Are you sure?

960
01:14:25.897 --> 01:14:30.057
I heard the shot and saw
Coleman standing there over him.

961
01:14:30.137 --> 01:14:32.017
It suits me, too.

962
01:14:33.817 --> 01:14:36.177
So he'll even do murder.

963
01:14:36.537 --> 01:14:39.357
And so I pronounce you man and wife.

964
01:14:39.437 --> 01:14:42.417
And may peace and happiness be yours.

965
01:14:42.497 --> 01:14:44.357
I like this prize.

966
01:14:47.557 --> 01:14:49.497
There's been a murder.

967
01:14:49.697 --> 01:14:50.697
Murder?

968
01:14:50.797 --> 01:14:52.057
Where? Where, girl?

969
01:14:52.137 --> 01:14:54.937
Who? Coleman left his throat
in the brush and shot him.

970
01:14:55.017 --> 01:14:57.337
That's a serious accusation, my girl.

971
01:14:57.417 --> 01:14:59.297
Are you sure? My brother saw it.

972
01:14:59.377 --> 01:15:02.717
Men, we can't have
cold-blooded murderers among us.

973
01:15:02.857 --> 01:15:05.897
There's a man who shot
Bill Thorpe down like a dog.

974
01:15:05.977 --> 01:15:07.917
Go and get a rope, Rupes. Get a rope.

975
01:15:07.997 --> 01:15:08.977
Yeah, get the rope.

976
01:15:09.057 --> 01:15:12.137
And just who accuses me of killing Thorpe?

977
01:15:13.457 --> 01:15:15.897
It was Miss Cameron.

978
01:15:18.677 --> 01:15:19.977
You, eh?

979
01:15:22.117 --> 01:15:24.557
So you'd like to see me hang?

980
01:15:31.057 --> 01:15:32.837
Listen to me, you!

981
01:15:33.657 --> 01:15:36.057
This boy Coleman here just
couldn't have killed Stone.

982
01:15:36.137 --> 01:15:38.717
Yeah, why not? Because he
didn't have no guns on him.

983
01:15:38.797 --> 01:15:41.557
He'd left his one with
Dutch Henry to be fixed.

984
01:15:41.637 --> 01:15:43.397
Thorpe heard odds over the Cameron gal.

985
01:15:43.477 --> 01:15:45.397
If it wasn't Coleman, who was it?

986
01:15:45.477 --> 01:15:49.457
Who shot Thorpe? Since you're so anxious
to know, I'll tell you who done it.

987
01:15:49.537 --> 01:15:52.257
Who? I shot that skunk myself.

988
01:15:52.817 --> 01:15:54.397
Coleman's a friend of his men.

989
01:15:54.477 --> 01:15:56.017
He's trying to save his neck.

990
01:15:56.097 --> 01:15:58.257
What could Zeke have
against a man like Thorpe?

991
01:15:58.337 --> 01:15:59.337
You want to know that, too?

992
01:15:59.417 --> 01:16:00.517
Yes, I want to know that, too.

993
01:16:00.597 --> 01:16:03.937
Well, I'm telling you. I was
camped out pretty close to you,

994
01:16:04.017 --> 01:16:07.457
and I heard that powwow
you had with Thorpe.

995
01:16:07.537 --> 01:16:08.697
Yeah, what are you driving at?

996
01:16:08.777 --> 01:16:09.757
Just this.

997
01:16:09.837 --> 01:16:13.617
When a man begins to do a lot of talking
about hanging, he'd better be pretty

998
01:16:13.697 --> 01:16:16.517
certain as to who's going to
decorate the end of that rope.

999
01:16:16.597 --> 01:16:19.317
Get my meaning? Well,
Thorpe ain't nothing to me.

1000
01:16:19.397 --> 01:16:22.617
It's no fair, mine. That's
just what I was to thinking.

1001
01:16:22.697 --> 01:16:26.337
Coleman ain't scouting for
any train that I'm bossing.

1002
01:16:26.417 --> 01:16:28.977
I'm leaving him behind.

1003
01:16:35.257 --> 01:16:36.477
Oh, no.

1004
01:16:36.557 --> 01:16:38.537
I've taken on a new scout.

1005
01:16:39.477 --> 01:16:41.417
Yes, again, Flack.

1006
01:16:41.717 --> 01:16:44.577
I started with this outfit,
and I'll be with it at the finish.

1007
01:16:44.657 --> 01:16:46.857
Who says so? I'm just telling you.

1008
01:16:46.937 --> 01:16:48.577
I got two reasons.

1009
01:16:48.917 --> 01:16:52.177
One is I told Wilmore I'd
scout the train through.

1010
01:16:53.097 --> 01:16:56.717
And the other is a little personal
business I aim to transact at the end of the

1011
01:16:56.797 --> 01:16:57.797
trail.

1012
01:16:58.097 --> 01:17:01.017
See if you can figure
out what that is, Flack.

1013
01:17:05.377 --> 01:17:08.957
Holman, the settlers
are willing to push on.

1014
01:17:10.177 --> 01:17:12.337
What's all this talk about engines?

1015
01:17:12.437 --> 01:17:13.437
It's true.

1016
01:17:13.517 --> 01:17:16.477
The engines are gathering to the
western to stop us from going through.

1017
01:17:16.557 --> 01:17:20.237
Engines have never yet prevented our breed
of men from traveling into the set and

1018
01:17:20.317 --> 01:17:20.877
sun.

1019
01:17:20.957 --> 01:17:22.637
Go on. Lead the way.

1020
01:17:22.717 --> 01:17:24.077
Well, get your outfits together.

1021
01:17:24.157 --> 01:17:25.297
We're going.

1022
01:17:27.917 --> 01:17:31.957
Never mind what you see or what you hear.

1023
01:17:32.037 --> 01:17:35.637
Red Flack is still boss of the train.

1024
01:17:36.097 --> 01:17:37.377
Get him on!

1025
01:17:40.377 --> 01:17:41.457
Come on, boy. Get up.

1026
01:17:41.537 --> 01:17:43.977
Come there. Come on.

1027
01:17:44.237 --> 01:17:45.497
Keep going.

1028
01:17:49.557 --> 01:17:50.737
Get up.

1029
01:18:10.597 --> 01:18:12.797
Ah-ha!

1030
01:19:07.317 --> 01:19:09.217
Oh,

1031
01:19:10.317 --> 01:19:12.577
what's all this?

1032
01:19:15.257 --> 01:19:17.017
Engine signs!

1033
01:19:17.877 --> 01:19:18.417
Corral!

1034
01:19:18.497 --> 01:19:19.677
Corral!

1035
01:20:04.617 --> 01:20:06.217
Hold up!

1036
01:21:04.297 --> 01:21:06.457
Oh, my God.

1037
01:21:27.677 --> 01:21:30.277
It's like crows and Cheyenne, Zeke.

1038
01:21:44.057 --> 01:21:45.957
Let's throw it into him.

1039
01:22:09.377 --> 01:22:12.837
Oh, my God.

1040
01:23:57.417 --> 01:24:01.177
I guess we were just a
little too much for them.

1041
01:24:15.657 --> 01:24:21.257
Father, our good friends have perished
here at the hands of the savages.

1042
01:24:21.457 --> 01:24:27.817
Open your arms to them and care for
our loved ones until we meet again on

1043
01:24:27.897 --> 01:24:29.137
the other shore.

1044
01:24:29.397 --> 01:24:30.437
Amen.

1045
01:24:32.117 --> 01:24:34.857
Old Wendy's gone on another trail.

1046
01:25:04.137 --> 01:25:07.897
I'm going to trail the engines and make
sure they go back to their villages.

1047
01:25:07.977 --> 01:25:09.757
Will you scout the train ahead?

1048
01:25:09.837 --> 01:25:11.937
I'll pick it up in a week or so.

1049
01:25:12.117 --> 01:25:13.457
Bye, Zeke.

1050
01:25:14.817 --> 01:25:16.077
Bye, boy.

1051
01:26:38.377 --> 01:26:39.657
I don't know.

1052
01:26:39.737 --> 01:26:42.517
I heard those three
wagons already turned back.

1053
01:26:42.597 --> 01:26:45.277
Ma, let's turn back to Missouri.

1054
01:26:45.357 --> 01:26:46.057
Me?

1055
01:26:46.137 --> 01:26:48.337
Turn back because of a little ma?

1056
01:26:48.417 --> 01:26:52.037
Sam, when did best some
women ever turn back?

1057
01:26:52.117 --> 01:26:55.797
Grandma, don't you and Ma
know that Pa's only joking?

1058
01:26:56.717 --> 01:26:58.617
All right, now, be pulling.

1059
01:26:58.817 --> 01:26:59.817
All right.

1060
01:27:04.477 --> 01:27:05.997
Come on, Dave.

1061
01:27:06.877 --> 01:27:07.977
Come on.

1062
01:27:08.097 --> 01:27:09.097
Come on.

1063
01:27:10.217 --> 01:27:13.837
Well, who would ever expect to
see Miss Cameron stuck in the mud?

1064
01:27:13.917 --> 01:27:15.797
We're all in the mud, Coleman.

1065
01:27:16.117 --> 01:27:19.037
I'll uncouple the wagons and
we'll pull them out one at a time,

1066
01:27:19.117 --> 01:27:19.617
Dave.

1067
01:27:19.657 --> 01:27:20.657
All right.

1068
01:27:21.097 --> 01:27:22.177
Pull them.

1069
01:27:34.877 --> 01:27:38.737
Oh, you idiot.

1070
01:27:38.817 --> 01:27:40.037
You see what you've done?

1071
01:27:40.117 --> 01:27:43.077
You've got my wagon up to the humping mud.

1072
01:27:43.357 --> 01:27:44.777
What are you kicking about?

1073
01:27:44.857 --> 01:27:46.837
I am sitting on my mule.

1074
01:27:47.477 --> 01:27:50.437
But don't worry, Mama.
I think it's going to clear up.

1075
01:27:50.517 --> 01:27:51.797
There will be no more rain.

1076
01:27:51.877 --> 01:27:53.017
Get up!

1077
01:27:53.097 --> 01:27:54.497
Get up! Throw that idiot!

1078
01:27:54.577 --> 01:27:57.097
Throw that idiot a rope
and help him out of there!

1079
01:27:57.177 --> 01:27:58.777
Get up!

1080
01:27:58.977 --> 01:28:01.037
Get up! Here, you hold it!

1081
01:29:53.217 --> 01:29:54.997
What did I tell you, eh?

1082
01:29:55.077 --> 01:29:56.577
You wouldn't listen to me.

1083
01:29:56.657 --> 01:29:58.397
You wouldn't listen to me.

1084
01:29:58.477 --> 01:30:02.057
Well, Lord, thou ain't a
man here that knows the past.

1085
01:30:02.137 --> 01:30:04.217
Over them hills, where?

1086
01:30:04.297 --> 01:30:05.817
But turn it back.

1087
01:30:06.477 --> 01:30:10.157
Please, please, men, follow me,

1088
01:30:11.577 --> 01:30:12.857
Coleman told us about.

1089
01:30:12.937 --> 01:30:14.177
Coleman, huh?

1090
01:30:14.257 --> 01:30:17.517
He's the only one that knows the way out.

1091
01:30:17.597 --> 01:30:20.037
And he is desolate us.

1092
01:30:20.117 --> 01:30:24.537
If he was here, I'd shoot
him down in his tracks.

1093
01:30:24.617 --> 01:30:26.337
Just when are you going
to start this shoot?

1094
01:30:26.417 --> 01:30:28.177
You're just in time, Coleman.

1095
01:30:28.257 --> 01:30:30.037
Did you find the Camerons?

1096
01:30:30.117 --> 01:30:32.297
They're over yonder.
What's the trouble here?

1097
01:30:32.377 --> 01:30:33.717
They're all against me.

1098
01:30:33.797 --> 01:30:35.117
They're turning back.

1099
01:30:35.977 --> 01:30:37.617
No, you're not.

1100
01:30:38.257 --> 01:30:40.317
We can't turn back.

1101
01:30:41.577 --> 01:30:43.377
The trail has started in England.

1102
01:30:43.457 --> 01:30:47.137
Not even the storms of the sea
could turn back those first settlers.

1103
01:30:47.217 --> 01:30:49.177
And they carried it on further.

1104
01:30:49.257 --> 01:30:52.357
They blazed it on through
the wilderness of Kentucky.

1105
01:30:52.437 --> 01:30:56.177
Famine, hunger, not even
massacres could stop them.

1106
01:30:56.277 --> 01:30:58.557
And now we've picked up the trail again.

1107
01:30:58.637 --> 01:31:00.797
And nothing can stop us.

1108
01:31:01.337 --> 01:31:05.037
Not even the snow, the winter, nor
the peaks of the highest mountains.

1109
01:31:05.117 --> 01:31:06.737
We're building a nation.

1110
01:31:06.817 --> 01:31:09.017
But we've got to stop it.

1111
01:31:09.737 --> 01:31:12.997
No great trail was ever
blazed without hardship.

1112
01:31:13.637 --> 01:31:15.377
And you've got to fight.

1113
01:31:15.617 --> 01:31:16.697
That's life.

1114
01:31:16.777 --> 01:31:19.757
And when you stop fighting, that's death.

1115
01:31:19.857 --> 01:31:22.737
What are you going to
do, lie down and die?

1116
01:31:22.957 --> 01:31:24.017
No!

1117
01:31:24.737 --> 01:31:26.737
Not in a thousand years.

1118
01:31:26.817 --> 01:31:28.457
You're going on with me.

1119
01:31:28.537 --> 01:31:31.537
The word is said and we'll follow you.

1120
01:31:31.617 --> 01:31:33.497
Be ready to start a gun up.

1121
01:31:41.297 --> 01:31:43.697
Well, he's turned up again.

1122
01:31:46.577 --> 01:31:48.757
He'll down the two of us, eh?

1123
01:31:48.837 --> 01:31:50.897
You've got to get him tonight.

1124
01:31:50.997 --> 01:31:52.917
No, they can hear a shot at night.

1125
01:31:52.997 --> 01:31:54.937
They can't hear a knife.

1126
01:31:55.057 --> 01:31:56.937
They all know this knife of mine.

1127
01:31:57.017 --> 01:31:59.877
Yeah, well, here is a knife.

1128
01:31:59.957 --> 01:32:01.377
They don't know.

1129
01:32:02.397 --> 01:32:03.837
No, no, no.

1130
01:32:03.937 --> 01:32:05.757
I'm afraid of that knife.

1131
01:32:06.037 --> 01:32:07.997
I know where you got it.

1132
01:32:08.617 --> 01:32:10.717
He'll get us in trouble, sure.

1133
01:32:10.797 --> 01:32:11.897
Yes, how?

1134
01:32:12.017 --> 01:32:15.237
Because a dead man's
knife is bad medicine.

1135
01:32:15.317 --> 01:32:17.097
Yeah, take this.

1136
01:32:17.177 --> 01:32:19.737
No. And watch for the night.

1137
01:32:25.617 --> 01:32:27.277
Frank, I have on here.

1138
01:32:27.357 --> 01:32:28.417
There he goes.

1139
01:32:33.257 --> 01:32:35.337
Wait until he's bedded down.

1140
01:32:35.417 --> 01:32:37.917
And then...

1141
01:32:47.757 --> 01:32:49.397
Give me a drink.

1142
01:32:52.017 --> 01:32:57.757
God bless my sister Ruth and my brother
Dave, and make me a good girl and take care

1143
01:32:57.837 --> 01:32:58.837
of us.

1144
01:33:00.737 --> 01:33:04.149
Aren't you going to ask God
to take care of Brett Coleman?

1145
01:33:05.417 --> 01:33:08.123
that Brett Coleman could
take care of himself.

1146
01:33:27.237 --> 01:33:30.597
You overplayed your hand that time, Lopez.

1147
01:33:46.137 --> 01:33:49.057
Zeke, this is old Ben Griswold's knife.

1148
01:33:50.617 --> 01:33:52.237
Where'd you find it, boys?

1149
01:33:52.317 --> 01:33:55.177
Lopez just left it sticking in my bedroll.

1150
01:33:55.537 --> 01:33:58.517
They're having it make the certain
that Black and Lopez did it.

1151
01:33:58.597 --> 01:34:00.197
No question about it, boys.

1152
01:34:00.277 --> 01:34:01.537
What did they do, Coleman?

1153
01:34:01.617 --> 01:34:03.037
Killed my best friend.

1154
01:34:03.117 --> 01:34:05.235
I've been on their trail ever since.

1155
01:34:06.357 --> 01:34:10.537
If you're sure, we'll call a settler's
meeting in the morning to try them.

1156
01:34:10.617 --> 01:34:12.817
You can call a settler's
meeting to bury them.

1157
01:34:12.897 --> 01:34:13.877
What do you mean?

1158
01:34:13.957 --> 01:34:15.797
That I kill my own rat.

1159
01:34:29.597 --> 01:34:31.177
They've jumped camp, Zeke.

1160
01:34:31.257 --> 01:34:33.237
And I'm off on their trail.

1161
01:34:33.537 --> 01:34:35.617
Coleman, you can't leave us here.

1162
01:34:35.697 --> 01:34:37.077
You've got to see us through.

1163
01:34:37.157 --> 01:34:38.617
He's right, boy.

1164
01:34:39.037 --> 01:34:41.397
Maybe so, the way you all look at it.

1165
01:34:41.477 --> 01:34:44.497
But those two men killed
a man in cold blood.

1166
01:34:44.577 --> 01:34:46.957
And they've got to pay.

1167
01:34:47.577 --> 01:34:50.077
Not that I've got hatred in my heart.

1168
01:34:50.237 --> 01:34:52.717
But it's that I'm the
law out here, that's all.

1169
01:34:52.797 --> 01:34:54.777
And the law is justice.

1170
01:34:57.477 --> 01:35:01.117
Well, Zeke, I'll see him
to the end of the trail.

1171
01:35:01.897 --> 01:35:04.757
But then I'm picking up a new trail here

1172
01:35:30.617 --> 01:35:31.377
Get over!

1173
01:35:31.457 --> 01:35:32.857
Get over!

1174
01:35:43.417 --> 01:35:46.457
You understand the Great White Mountain.

1175
01:35:47.277 --> 01:35:50.657
And down there is the
valley I've told you about.

1176
01:35:50.737 --> 01:35:53.477
Coleman, you have fulfilled our hopes.

1177
01:35:55.097 --> 01:35:56.277
Friends,

1178
01:35:56.557 --> 01:35:57.557
neighbors,

1179
01:35:57.977 --> 01:36:02.037
It is fitting that we give
thanks to the Almighty.

1180
01:36:04.837 --> 01:36:09.897
Our Father, we thank Thee for
leading us to this land of promise,

1181
01:36:09.977 --> 01:36:14.217
for guiding our footsteps safely
through the dangers of our pilgrimage.

1182
01:36:14.377 --> 01:36:18.097
In this valley of our dreams,
we'll build our home and serve Thee,

1183
01:36:18.177 --> 01:36:22.777
O Father, and our children's
children shall praise Thy name.

1184
01:36:22.857 --> 01:36:23.957
Amen.

1185
01:36:24.257 --> 01:36:26.597
The way lies clear ahead.

1186
01:36:27.037 --> 01:36:28.497
All gentle slopes.

1187
01:36:29.077 --> 01:36:31.477
So drive down, my friends, and settle it.

1188
01:36:31.557 --> 01:36:32.817
Lead the way.

1189
01:36:33.457 --> 01:36:35.437
Zeke will lead the way down.

1190
01:36:35.917 --> 01:36:37.697
Our trail's forked here.

1191
01:36:37.777 --> 01:36:39.657
You mean you're leaving us?

1192
01:36:39.797 --> 01:36:43.797
There's a trail I've followed
for over 3,000 miles now.

1193
01:36:43.877 --> 01:36:48.297
And I'm heading back to pick it
up again and follow it to the end.

1194
01:36:49.797 --> 01:36:54.017
Coleman, you're the breed of man
that would follow a trail to the end.

1195
01:36:54.097 --> 01:36:55.577
Thanks, Bascom.

1196
01:36:57.037 --> 01:36:58.017
You killed one.

1197
01:36:58.097 --> 01:37:00.817
Boy, there's two of them.

1198
01:37:00.897 --> 01:37:02.077
And they're bad.

1199
01:37:02.157 --> 01:37:04.177
Now I'm going with you.

1200
01:37:05.257 --> 01:37:06.757
No, Zeke.

1201
01:37:07.377 --> 01:37:10.437
You stay here and take
care of Ruth and her outfit.

1202
01:37:19.477 --> 01:37:21.657
Rick, you're not leaving.

1203
01:37:21.997 --> 01:37:23.817
Yes, Miss Ruth, I'm pulling out.

1204
01:37:23.897 --> 01:37:27.677
They say you're going to
hunt down Flack and Lopez.

1205
01:37:27.817 --> 01:37:29.097
That's what I aim to do.

1206
01:37:29.177 --> 01:37:31.157
But you can't do this awful thing.

1207
01:37:31.237 --> 01:37:32.977
Take two lives.

1208
01:37:34.157 --> 01:37:35.657
Frontier justice.

1209
01:37:36.517 --> 01:37:38.697
Don't go, Brack. Don't go.

1210
01:37:39.237 --> 01:37:41.737
It's a job I've got to finish.

1211
01:37:42.917 --> 01:37:44.377
Don't you see?

1212
01:37:44.677 --> 01:37:46.577
It doesn't matter about them.

1213
01:37:46.657 --> 01:37:48.397
I'm afraid for you.

1214
01:37:48.737 --> 01:37:50.357
They'll kill you.

1215
01:37:53.897 --> 01:37:56.797
You're everything in the world to me, Rex.

1216
01:37:57.337 --> 01:37:59.097
I can't let you go.

1217
01:37:59.177 --> 01:38:00.477
I can't.

1218
01:38:02.797 --> 01:38:05.157
The thing has to be done.

1219
01:38:07.777 --> 01:38:08.957
Someday,

1220
01:38:10.417 --> 01:38:11.597
somewhere,

1221
01:38:12.417 --> 01:38:14.817
our trails will cross again.

1222
01:38:21.397 --> 01:38:23.017
Now, now.

1223
01:38:23.097 --> 01:38:24.737
Come. coming, miss.

1224
01:38:24.817 --> 01:38:27.597
You mustn't be carrying on that away.

1225
01:38:28.097 --> 01:38:29.437
He's gone.

1226
01:38:30.137 --> 01:38:31.697
He'll never come back.

1227
01:38:31.777 --> 01:38:34.897
Now, now, you just mustn't do this, miss.

1228
01:38:35.177 --> 01:38:37.957
You'll have me a blubber
in here pretty soon.

1229
01:38:38.217 --> 01:38:41.717
I'm telling you that everything
is going to be all right.

1230
01:38:41.797 --> 01:38:46.477
When spring comes in that valley,
he'll be tracking back again.

1231
01:38:46.557 --> 01:38:48.537
I know that, boy.

1232
01:38:48.757 --> 01:38:50.477
I know him.

1233
01:38:50.697 --> 01:38:52.917
Now, come, come.

1234
01:38:52.997 --> 01:38:54.117
Come on.

1235
01:38:58.997 --> 01:39:00.897
Object.

1236
01:39:33.497 --> 01:39:36.137
My legs are closed to the knees.

1237
01:39:37.137 --> 01:39:38.497
I can't get up.

1238
01:39:38.577 --> 01:39:41.197
Yes, looks as if you're done for, Lopez.

1239
01:39:42.537 --> 01:39:44.477
Don't go away and leave me, Frank.

1240
01:39:44.557 --> 01:39:47.517
What? You think I'm staying here?

1241
01:39:47.857 --> 01:39:49.637
Then leave me a blanket.

1242
01:39:49.717 --> 01:39:51.337
Don't do you no good.

1243
01:39:51.417 --> 01:39:53.817
You'll be froze to death in an hour.

1244
01:39:53.897 --> 01:39:55.417
Hey, help me!

1245
01:39:55.497 --> 01:39:57.077
I'll get away! Black!

1246
01:39:57.157 --> 01:39:58.337
Black!

1247
01:39:59.597 --> 01:40:01.057
Don't let me die!

1248
01:40:01.137 --> 01:40:02.317
I'll hold you!

1249
01:40:02.557 --> 01:40:03.957
Stay with me!

1250
01:40:05.157 --> 01:40:06.397
Get out of here!

1251
01:40:34.617 --> 01:40:36.317
Well, Lopez,

1252
01:40:36.737 --> 01:40:39.397
it won't be long before you have company.

1253
01:41:22.997 --> 01:41:27.057
Oh, my God.

1254
01:42:07.037 --> 01:42:08.617
Now, wait a little bit.

1255
01:42:25.857 --> 01:42:26.877
Yeah,

1256
01:42:28.917 --> 01:42:33.457
well, Cedric, I got a hankering
to trail on down into Mexico.

1257
01:42:34.097 --> 01:42:39.937
Old Bill Gillis' son told me them
black-eyed gals is just full of fire.

1258
01:42:40.197 --> 01:42:41.657
Zeke. Yeah.

1259
01:42:41.777 --> 01:42:43.677
You're not really leaving us.

1260
01:42:43.757 --> 01:42:45.597
Yeah, gal, I'm a puller now.

1261
01:42:45.837 --> 01:42:48.437
You was all nice and settled now.

1262
01:42:48.597 --> 01:42:51.377
This dolly's getting too civilized for me.

1263
01:42:51.517 --> 01:42:54.657
Whenever I get more than three or four
families within a hundred mile of me,

1264
01:42:54.737 --> 01:42:56.797
I begin to feel kind of crowded.

1265
01:42:57.517 --> 01:42:59.657
That's not why you're going, Zeke.

1266
01:42:59.737 --> 01:43:01.437
Oh, for else, gal.

1267
01:43:01.517 --> 01:43:02.517
Well,

1268
01:43:03.357 --> 01:43:05.257
Breck has never come back.

1269
01:43:06.157 --> 01:43:07.797
You're going out to look for him.

1270
01:43:07.877 --> 01:43:12.177
Now, wherever that boy Breck Coleman
is at, he's looking out for himself.

1271
01:43:12.257 --> 01:43:14.537
Now, don't you fret about him.

1272
01:43:24.917 --> 01:43:27.957
Sophie, did you give all
your little puppies away?

1273
01:43:34.437 --> 01:43:36.797
Why are you looking at that dress?

1274
01:43:39.117 --> 01:43:44.197
This is the anniversary of the day
that the wagon train left from Missouri.

1275
01:43:45.757 --> 01:43:51.077
Last time I had this on,
I was sitting in the Riggs cabin.

1276
01:43:51.157 --> 01:43:52.777
In a rocking chair?

1277
01:43:53.957 --> 01:43:55.657
Yes, honey girl.

1278
01:43:56.677 --> 01:43:58.737
In a rocking chair.

1279
01:44:08.377 --> 01:44:10.657
Zeke, I recognize the panther.

1280
01:44:10.737 --> 01:44:12.957
Yeah, a two-legged panther.

1281
01:44:13.037 --> 01:44:17.037
The only kind will ever give me
that Comanche yell as a signal.

1282
01:44:17.117 --> 01:44:20.477
We might just as well start to unpack.

1283
01:44:21.097 --> 01:44:22.657
What, ain't you going?

1284
01:44:22.737 --> 01:44:24.297
No use to go on now.

1285
01:44:24.377 --> 01:44:27.817
He's up in the timber a bit,
and he's ahead of his way.

1286
01:44:28.057 --> 01:44:30.997
Zeke, won't you stay
over for the anniversary?

1287
01:44:31.517 --> 01:44:32.797
Gal, I'll stay.

1288
01:44:32.877 --> 01:44:34.237
And I just recollected.

1289
01:44:34.317 --> 01:44:36.257
I got a little perfect for you.

1290
01:44:36.337 --> 01:44:40.277
Oh, Zeke, what is it? Well, a young fellow
named Brett Coleman left it with me.

1291
01:44:40.357 --> 01:44:43.857
And he told me to give it to
you in case he didn't show up.

1292
01:44:44.317 --> 01:44:49.437
Where is it, Zeke? I hid it in the hollow
of the big tree at the bend of the trail.

1293
01:44:49.557 --> 01:44:51.217
You'll find it there.

1294
01:44:52.097 --> 01:44:53.337
Thanks, Zeke.

1295
01:44:53.597 --> 01:44:55.097
I'll go get it.

1296
01:45:02.377 --> 01:45:05.637
Thank you.

